BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Come From Away: Marin's First Production of the Tony-Winning Music
 al
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T210000
UID:261108yI3RXpE16kyE3zuTf1cbKw
DESCRIPTION:A Tony-winning Broadway hit is coming to San Anselmo\, and it'
 s the first time it's ever been performed in Marin.\n\nCome From Away\n\nB
 ook\, Music and Lyrics by Irene Sankoff and David Hein\n\nOn 9/11\, 38 pla
 nes were suddenly grounded in a tiny town in Newfoundland. Overnight\, the
  locals took in nearly 7\,000 stranded travelers from around the world\, a
 nd strangers became family. This is their true story\, and it's funny\, up
 lifting and full of heart\, with a live band of musicians from Marin's Iri
 sh music scene.\n\nSan Domenico School's production marks the 25th anniver
 sary of 9/11.\n\nShow times:\n\nFriday\, November 13 at 7pm\n\nSaturday\, 
 November 14 at 1pm and 7pm\n\nSunday\, November 15 at 3pm\n\nTickets: $15 
 general\, $10 students and seniors\n\nRun time: About 2 hours\, including 
 intermission\n\nFree parking. Wheelchair accessible.\n\nSaturday night sti
 ll has the best seats!\n\nPlease be advised that adult language and the me
 ntion of difficult subject matter\, including Islamophobia and 9/11\, are 
 included in this show.\n\nCome From Away is presented through special arra
 ngement with Music Theatre International \\(MTI\\). MTI also supplies all 
 authorized performance materials. www.MTIShows.com
LOCATION:Carol Franc Buck Hall of the Arts\, San Domenico School
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-f
 rom-away-tickets-2003472917428
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
