BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Autumn Twilight: A Candlelighgt Sound Bath
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T164500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T180000
UID:261107J17IoI8XSEa0Jc_NpGmpIQ
DESCRIPTION:🍂 Autumn Twilight: A Candlelight Sound Bath Experience\n\nJ
 ourney Beyond Sound’s final floating gathering of 2026 is moving indoors
 ! With rain expected\, we’re bringing the experience into the community 
 room at Terra Linda Community Center\, with a new start time of 6:00 PM.\n
 \nRelax on a luxury air mattress as live musicians serenade you with gongs
 \, singing bowls\, drums\, native instruments\, and nature soundscapes. Ca
 ndles will line the room as the music carries you into a gentler\, softer 
 space. 🎶\n\nWe’ll gently guide you through an opening meditation\, th
 en let the music do the journeying. Wrap yourself in a blanket and settle 
 into an evening of candlelight\, live sound\, and a little room to float i
 nward.\n\nLuxury air mattress spots are limited\, and these experiences te
 nd to sell out early.\n\nSaturday\, November 14\, 2026 · 6:00 PM Terra Li
 nda Community Center\, Community Room 670 Del Ganado Road\, San Rafael\, C
 A 94903\n\n$65 admission includes a personal luxury air mattress for the e
 xperience. Tickets\, what to bring\, and complete details are available th
 rough Eventbrite and JourneyBeyondSound.com.
LOCATION:Terra Linda Community Center
URL:https://journeybeyondsound.com/etn/autumn-twilight-floating-sound-bath
 -terra-linda-san-rafael/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Choose Your Own Adventure - Public Hikes at Fairfield Osborn Prese
 rve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T140000
UID:261105Q0RTpXUhcEep6Q_6YK_VZQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us to explore the lands of Fairfield Osborn Preserve with
  trained naturalists. "Choose Your Own Adventure" with University students
  and community docents who will lead your hike on one of many trails into 
 this 450-acre preserve on the shoulder of Sonoma Mountain. Our guides are 
 trained in the natural history of the mountain and interpretation of prese
 rve programs. Hike options include visits to the headwaters of Copeland Cr
 eek and spectacular vistas of the Santa Rosa Valley and Valley of the Moon
LOCATION:Fairfield Osborn Preserve
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/choose-your-own-adventure-fall2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artazan Handcraft Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T170000
UID:261104f2NogPjgekaTtSopOJIGAQ
DESCRIPTION:Artazan Handcraft Market returns to Pasadena November 14–15\
 , bringing together artists\, artisans\, craftspeople and the community fo
 r a weekend celebrating creativity and work made by hand.\n\nInspired by t
 he ideas behind the Arts & Crafts movement\, the handcraft market celebrat
 es creativity\, thoughtful design\, skilled work and the people behind the
  things we bring into our lives. That spirit is reflected in a contemporar
 y and wide-ranging mix of handcraft\, encompassing many different material
 s\, traditions and creative approaches.\n\nHeld at the Pasadena Convention
  Center\, the two-day market will be filled with work from independent art
 ists and artisans across an eclectic mix of mediums. Visitors might discov
 er jewelry and metalsmithing\, ceramics and glass\, crochet and fiber art\
 , woodworking and handcrafted clocks\, painting and mixed media\, wearable
  art\, leatherwork\, home décor\, artisan foods and much more. From time-
 honored skills to unexpected new ideas\, the market reflects the remarkabl
 e variety of what people are creating by hand today.\n\nThe weekend will a
 lso connect with Pasadena’s broader creative community\, bringing togeth
 er local and regional artists\, arts organizations\, educators and visitor
 s. Guests can talk directly with artists\, learn about their materials and
  techniques\, take part in hands-on workshops\, watch demonstrations and e
 njoy live music throughout the weekend.\n\nTaking place at the beginning o
 f the holiday season\, the November market offers an alternative to mass-p
 roduced holiday shopping\, with distinctive gifts\, original art\, artisan
  foods and objects for the home\, while directly supporting independent ar
 tists and small creative businesses.\n\nMore than a place to shop\, Artaza
 n offers an opportunity to see handcraft up close\, discover something une
 xpected and experience the incredible range of things being made by hand t
 oday.\n\n**EVENT DETAILS Artazan Handcraft Market** November 14–15\, 202
 6 Pasadena Convention Center • Pasadena\, California Saturday & Sunday 
 • 10 a.m.–5 p.m.\n\nTickets\, workshops\, exhibitor information and ad
 ditional details are available at **Artazan.com**.
LOCATION:Pasadena Convention Center
URL:https://www.artazan.com/pasadena.php
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
