BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Veterans Holiday Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T160000
UID:2609301cNzEsQXRE6FDIxoAwL3wQ
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma VFW Auxiliary Post 1943 will host its **4th Annual 
 Veterans Holiday Market** on Saturday\, November 14\, from 10 a.m. to 4 p.
 m.\, and Sunday\, November 15\, from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m. at the Veterans Mem
 orial Building\, 126 First St. West\, Sonoma.\n\nThe two-day holiday marke
 t will feature one-of-a-kind\, limited-edition goods handcrafted by local 
 artists and makers. With several vendors participating\, shoppers will hav
 e an opportunity to find unique gifts while supporting the Auxiliary’s m
 ission of helping those who have served and their loved ones.\n\nThe Nativ
 e Daughters of the Golden West\, Sonoma Parlor No. 209\, will also host a 
 special community activity\, **“Make a Veteran a Christmas Card.”** Co
 mmunity members of all ages are invited to create handmade holiday cards t
 hat will be delivered to area veterans living in assisted living facilitie
 s and nursing homes.\n\nThe Veterans Holiday Market is **free and open to 
 the public**\, with a special invitation extended to military members\, ve
 terans and their families. Proceeds from the event will help provide assis
 tance to veterans and military families who are experiencing hardship.\n\n
 The VFW Auxiliary is an all-volunteer service organization whose members i
 nclude the spouses\, parents\, grandparents\, brothers\, sisters and other
  family members of those who have served in overseas combat. Since 1934\, 
 members of Sonoma VFW Auxiliary Post 1943 have worked to support those who
  have served and strengthen the community around them.\n\nThe Auxiliary’
 s community service efforts have included toy and monetary donations to To
 ys for Tots\, Christmas gifts and cards for veterans at the Yountville Vet
 erans Home\, as well as clothing and food drives benefiting local emergenc
 y service organizations.\n\nThe Veterans Holiday Market is an opportunity 
 for the entire community to come together during the holiday season—not 
 only to shop and celebrate\, but also to show appreciation for those who h
 ave served and to remind veterans and their loved ones that they are value
 d\, remembered and not alone.\n\n**Veteran Families Helping Veterans**\n\n
 **For more information contact: Debbie Chandler (707)364-2734**
LOCATION:Sonoma Veterans Building
URL:http://vfwpost1943.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Western Swing Night with The Dogweeds
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T220000
UID:260929dE7DeorYL0KBvyTdifwmXQ
DESCRIPTION:Get on your cowboy boots\, grab your honey and come out to the
  Napa Grange for a great evening of Western Swing with The Dogweeds!\n\nDB
  Productions and the Welcome Grange bring another great evening of live mu
 sic to Napa. The Dogweeds draw inspiration from the Western Swing dance ba
 nds of the 1930's and 40's\, but with a modern take. Blazing instrumentals
  and honest\, soulful vocal harmonies meet dance-inspiring grooves in a so
 und that is both unique and familiar. Genre bending originals add elements
  of jazz\, blues\, vintage pop and folk\, while dazzling new arrangements 
 bring old classics and deep cuts to life.\n\n"Lyrics to make you think\, b
 ut music to make you move... " Rachel Cholst\, Adobe and Teardrops\n\n"red
 -hot musicianship and a genuine love for Western Swing - proof that the ge
 nre thrives in the hands of the next generation." Mae McCoy\, Western Swin
 g Society
LOCATION:Napa Welcome Grange
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/western-swing-dance-concert-with-the-dogw
 eeds-tickets-1999737350246?aff=oddtdtcreator#location
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Echoes of Innocence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T213000
UID:2609294LXoRt0qokWmc6Z8QqO74Q
DESCRIPTION:Echoes of Innocence\n\nNovember 14\, 15 & 16\, 2026\n\nWeill H
 all\, Green Music Center\n\n**Francesco Lecce-Chong\,** conductor\n\n**Oli
 ver Herbert\,** cello\n\n**Elisa Sunshine\,** soprano\n\n**SERGEI RACHMANI
 NOFF:** *Vocalise* in E minor for Soprano and Orchestra\, Opus 34\, No. 14
  **CAMILLE SAINT-SAËNS:** Concerto No. 1 in A minor for Cello and Orchest
 ra\, Opus 33 **GUSTAV MAHLER:** Symphony No. 4 in G major for Soprano and 
 Orchestra\n\nRachmaninoff’s *Vocalise* is a landmark piece of wordless l
 onging and quiet intensity. Bay Area native Oliver Herbert performs Saint-
 Saëns’ Cello Concerto No. 1\, a work that unfolds in a single continuou
 s movement\, shifting seamlessly between urgency and repose. Closing the p
 erformance\, Mahler’s ethereal Symphony No. 4 features a soprano in its 
 final movement\, which delivers a radiant and transcendent ending.\n\n**Pr
 ograms\, artists\, dates\, and prices are subject to change without notice
 . Tickets are subject to availability. All Tickets are nonrefundable.**\n\
 nPhoto by Todd Rosenberg
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/echoes-of-innocence/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bel Canto - The Art of the Aria
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T160000
UID:260922vN30-33u2U-j6g9YhGkKhQ
DESCRIPTION:Spend an afternoon immersed in some of the world’s most beau
 tiful arias\, featuring beloved works by master composers of the operatic 
 world. Experience the passion\, drama\, and beauty of opera through unforg
 ettable melodies and powerful voices. This special program brings together
  timeless selections that have captivated audiences for generations. Join 
 us for an afternoon of extraordinary music and a celebration of the operat
 ic tradition.
LOCATION:Haraszthy Villa at Bartholomew Estate
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/bel-canto-the-art-of-the-aria/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jerry Seinfeld
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T200000
UID:2609210fNC9Yt5k0Sc-JmOQfclTQ
DESCRIPTION:Jerry Seinfeld has been hailed for his uncanny ability to joke
  about the little things in life that relate to audiences everywhere. His 
 latest Emmy®-nominated Netflix projects include Jerry Before Seinfeld a
 nd 23 Hours to Kill\, along with the highly acclaimed web series\, Com
 edians in Cars Getting Coffee. Seinfeld has also starred in\, written\, a
 nd produced movies \\(Comedian\, Bee Movie\\)\, directed and produced a
  Broadway hit \\(Colin Quinn: Long Story Short\\)\, and wrote three bes
 t-selling books \\(Is This Anything?\, The Comedians in Cars Getting Co
 ffee Book\, and Seinlanguage\\) and a children’s book \\(Halloween\\).
  He stars in the Emmy-nominated comedy film\, Unfrosted\, which he dir
 ected\, co-wrote\, and produced. Seinfeld continues to perform both nat
 ionally and internationally.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/jerry-seinfeld26/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
