BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Guided Nature Walk & Ranch House tour Anderson Marsh State Histori
 c Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T103000
UID:261113rB4U3hQwdUC3XY1xjPPPfw
DESCRIPTION:The final Guided Nature Walk of 2026 at Anderson Marsh State H
 istoric Park will be held on Saturday\, November 14th beginning at 8:30am.
  The autumn season brings bright clear days and a chance to experience the
  fall bird migration that is in full swing at the park. \n\nThe Guided Wal
 k will be led by State Parks volunteer docent and California Naturalist He
 nry Bornstein\, who has been leading guided walks in the park for almost 2
 0 years. The guided walk provides an opportunity to observe wildlife at th
 e park and learn about their natural habitat\, as well as to learn about t
 he natural and cultural history of the area. \n\nAfter the Guided Walk\, t
 here will be an opportunity to tour the historic Anderson Ranch House. \n\
 nThe Guided Walk will begin at 8:30am. Bring binoculars and meet in the pa
 rking lot at 8:15am for an opportunity to observe the birds and other wild
 life found in the picnic area. Sturdy shoes\, a hat and water are suggeste
 d. \n\nThe walk will take between 1½ and 2 hours\, depending on the route
  taken. Steady rain will cancel the walk. Dogs are not allowed on the park
  trails\, which pass through the protected Anderson Marsh Nature Reserve. 
 The Ranch House tour will begin immediately after the conclusion of the Gu
 ided Walk. \n\nThere is no charge for the Nature Walk and Ranch House tour
  and parking is free for those attending. \n\nFor more information about t
 he guided walk\, email info@andersonmarsh.org
LOCATION:Anderson Marsh State Historic Park
URL:https://lakecounty.com/event/guided-nature-walk-ranch-house-tour-ander
 son-marsh-state-historic-park/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
