BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:When Teddy Roosevelt called Jack London a "Nature Faker"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T170000
UID:261019ajU2mbpmxki847mwQPku-A
DESCRIPTION:The "nature-faker" controversy between Jack London and Teddy R
 oosevelt was a public argument in the press after Roosevelt accused London
  of anthropomorphizing animals. While these two men might have publicly de
 bated\, they actually had a lot in common. Learn about how the Roosevelt f
 amily was involved in anti-animal cruelty advocacy\, including the foundin
 g of the A.S.P.C.A.\, how the "teddy bear" came about\, and how Jack Londo
 n's response to Roosevelt's criticism echoed much of what we would later u
 nderstand about animal cognition. Presented by Kate Johnston\, docent at t
 he Jack London Historic State Park. Kate is a retired government attorney 
 who writes a docent newsletter for the park. Her articles are featured on 
 the Jack London Society webpage. jacklondonsociety.org walksandtalksbykate
 .com
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Library
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/jack-london-118325
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
