BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blithe Spirit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
UID:261104ezrWqY66NkKv66ek1klzpA
DESCRIPTION:A ghostly comedy filled with unexpected twists\, supernatural 
 surprises\, and plenty of laughs is coming to the San Marin stage!\n\nSan 
 Marin Performing Arts is excited to present *Blithe Spirit*\, the classic 
 comedy by celebrated playwright Noël Coward. Running November 12–16 at 
 the Emily Gates Performing Arts Center\, this witty and spirited productio
 n brings together mystery\, mischief\, and a little supernatural chaos\, a
 ll brought to life by San Marin High School's talented drama students.\n\n
 About the Show\n\nWhat happens when a séance goes hilariously wrong?\n\nN
 ovelist Charles Condomine invites the eccentric medium Madame Arcati to hi
 s home\, hoping to gather inspiration for his next book. But when the séa
 nce unexpectedly summons the ghost of his first wife\, Elvira\, things qui
 ckly spiral out of control.\n\nInvisible to everyone but Charles\, the mis
 chievous Elvira is determined to disrupt his marriage to his second wife\,
  Ruth. As supernatural surprises and romantic rivalries unfold\, Charles f
 inds himself caught between two wives\, one living and one very much not.\
 n\nFilled with sharp dialogue\, clever humor\, and delightfully chaotic si
 tuations\, *Blithe Spirit* is a timeless comedy that proves some relations
 hips are difficult to leave behind\, even after death.\n\nMeet the Cast\n\
 n**Flint Berberich** as Charles Condomine\n\n**Jade Stanton** as Ruth Cond
 omine\n\n**Devyn Lawrence-Hall** as Elvira Condomine\n\n**Bella Lessig** a
 s Madame Arcati\n\n**Giselle De Leon** as Dr. George Bradman\n\n**Catania 
 DeKeyrel** as Mrs. Violet Bradman\n\n**Cailey Gettle and Amiya Clark** as 
 Edith\n\nPerformance Dates & Times\n\nJoin us for one of four performances
 :\n\n**Thursday\, November 12** — 7:00 PM\n\n**Friday\, November 13** 
 — 7:00 PM\n\n**Sunday\, November 15** — 2:00 PM\n\n**Monday\, November
  16** — 7:00 PM\n\n**Location:** Emily Gates Performing Arts Center\, Sa
 n Marin High School\, Novato\, CA\n\n**Co-Directed by Brad Smith and Linda
  Kislingbury**\n\nTickets & Admission\n\n**General Admission: $5 Students 
 / $10 Adults** General seating / Opening Seating. No reserved seats.\n\nTi
 ckets will be available for purchase at the door beginning one hour before
  each performance. Come enjoy an entertaining evening (or afternoon!) of l
 ive theater while supporting the talented student actors and crew who brin
 g this spirited comedy to the stage. We look forward to seeing you there!
LOCATION:Emily Gates Performing Arts Center - San Marin High
URL:https://www.sanmarinperformingarts.org/news-highlights/blithe-spirit
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artazan Handcraft Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:261104WfcMWeThTkSKmWHgt066Pw
DESCRIPTION:Artazan Handcraft Market returns to Pasadena November 14–15\
 , bringing together artists\, artisans\, craftspeople and the community fo
 r a weekend celebrating creativity and work made by hand.\n\nInspired by t
 he ideas behind the Arts & Crafts movement\, the handcraft market celebrat
 es creativity\, thoughtful design\, skilled work and the people behind the
  things we bring into our lives. That spirit is reflected in a contemporar
 y and wide-ranging mix of handcraft\, encompassing many different material
 s\, traditions and creative approaches.\n\nHeld at the Pasadena Convention
  Center\, the two-day market will be filled with work from independent art
 ists and artisans across an eclectic mix of mediums. Visitors might discov
 er jewelry and metalsmithing\, ceramics and glass\, crochet and fiber art\
 , woodworking and handcrafted clocks\, painting and mixed media\, wearable
  art\, leatherwork\, home décor\, artisan foods and much more. From time-
 honored skills to unexpected new ideas\, the market reflects the remarkabl
 e variety of what people are creating by hand today.\n\nThe weekend will a
 lso connect with Pasadena’s broader creative community\, bringing togeth
 er local and regional artists\, arts organizations\, educators and visitor
 s. Guests can talk directly with artists\, learn about their materials and
  techniques\, take part in hands-on workshops\, watch demonstrations and e
 njoy live music throughout the weekend.\n\nTaking place at the beginning o
 f the holiday season\, the November market offers an alternative to mass-p
 roduced holiday shopping\, with distinctive gifts\, original art\, artisan
  foods and objects for the home\, while directly supporting independent ar
 tists and small creative businesses.\n\nMore than a place to shop\, Artaza
 n offers an opportunity to see handcraft up close\, discover something une
 xpected and experience the incredible range of things being made by hand t
 oday.\n\n**EVENT DETAILS Artazan Handcraft Market** November 14–15\, 202
 6 Pasadena Convention Center • Pasadena\, California Saturday & Sunday 
 • 10 a.m.–5 p.m.\n\nTickets\, workshops\, exhibitor information and ad
 ditional details are available at **Artazan.com**.
LOCATION:Pasadena Convention Center
URL:https://www.artazan.com/pasadena.php
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Richard Heinberg: A Celebration of His Life and Legacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:261103bREdWt_gOEeeIiCBo7oJBA
DESCRIPTION:Author • Musician • Senior Fellow at Post Carbon Institute
  • Environmental Educator • Artist • Husband • Friend\n\nYou are w
 armly invited to join family\, friends\, colleagues\, and admirers from ar
 ound the world on November 15th as we come together to celebrate the extra
 ordinary life and legacy of Richard Heinberg.\n\nA Senior Fellow at Post C
 arbon Institute for nearly 20 years\, Richard was a pioneering voice on re
 silience and the energy crisis. He was the author of fourteen books\, hund
 reds of articles\, and the award-winning monthly Museletter.\n\nRichard wa
 s a skilled writer and speaker who could synthesize complex issues and ide
 as into understandable language. His calm demeanor\, sharp wit\, and inten
 se focus made difficult and daunting facts feel bearable.\n\nRichard was a
  lifelong violinist and guitarist who\, more recently\, took up the piano.
  For decades\, he maintained a devoted\, focused daily practice and played
  in bands\, chamber groups\, duos\, and orchestras throughout his life.\n\
 nBeyond his public work\, those who knew him personally were struck by his
  genuine curiosity. He was always asking questions and truly listening for
  the answers.  \n\nJoin us in Santa Rosa on November 15th for an afternoo
 n of gratitude and celebration for a life so fully and generously lived. R
 ichard’s commemoration will be held from 2:30 to 4:00 pm\, with arrival 
 starting at 2:00 pm and a social hour to follow the program.\n\nSeating is
  limited. Please use the RSVP link on EverLoved to save your spot.
LOCATION:See EverLoved for venue information
URL:https://everloved.com/life-of/richard-heinberg/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Misner & Smith Matinee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:261031bVUi234JjUSUChsP-7EO-Q
DESCRIPTION:Misner & Smith's music is a rare combination of poetic\, story
 -filled songwriting lifted to exquisite heights by masterful vocal harmoni
 es.\n\nFollowing the release of their critically acclaimed new album\, All
  is Song\, Northern California-based unclassifiable duo Misner & Smith ret
 urn to HopMonk Sebastopol - The Abbey - for another evening of masterful v
 ocal harmonies and extraordinary songwriting. With All is Song they turn i
 n their finest work to date--an album of inspired declarations to the powe
 r of music\, song\, and collaboration. Their live shows are no different\,
  and the beauty of their vocal harmonies combined with truly inventive son
 gwriting has made the band one of the most inspiring acts in the Americana
  world. Blending elements of that genre with rock\, traditional folk\, and
  more pop-leaning ideas\, Misner & Smith makes music gloriously nonconform
 ing.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040036054?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
