UID:261029Pvok4hPMLUqOcRT4yt2fwA
DESCRIPTION:Chamber Choir\, Circa 1600 has the pleasure of turning forward
  in the Old Testament and stepping into the mystical garden of the Song of
  Songs. Filled with longing\, sensuality\, and memorable imagery\, it’s 
 no wonder that this sacred poetry inspired many composers to write such ex
 pressive music. We will explore motets by composers close to our heart inc
 luding Giovanni Pierluigi da Palestrina\, Tomás Luis de Victoria\, and Ja
 cobus Clemens non Papa as well as lesser-known gems\, including the wonder
 ful *Missa Ego flos campi* by Juan Gutiérrez de Padilla.
LOCATION:Green Music Center
