BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blithe Spirit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T190000
UID:261104o10ZLwzMCE6-1s19INgTGA
DESCRIPTION:A ghostly comedy filled with unexpected twists\, supernatural 
 surprises\, and plenty of laughs is coming to the San Marin stage!\n\nSan 
 Marin Performing Arts is excited to present *Blithe Spirit*\, the classic 
 comedy by celebrated playwright Noël Coward. Running November 12–16 at 
 the Emily Gates Performing Arts Center\, this witty and spirited productio
 n brings together mystery\, mischief\, and a little supernatural chaos\, a
 ll brought to life by San Marin High School's talented drama students.\n\n
 About the Show\n\nWhat happens when a séance goes hilariously wrong?\n\nN
 ovelist Charles Condomine invites the eccentric medium Madame Arcati to hi
 s home\, hoping to gather inspiration for his next book. But when the séa
 nce unexpectedly summons the ghost of his first wife\, Elvira\, things qui
 ckly spiral out of control.\n\nInvisible to everyone but Charles\, the mis
 chievous Elvira is determined to disrupt his marriage to his second wife\,
  Ruth. As supernatural surprises and romantic rivalries unfold\, Charles f
 inds himself caught between two wives\, one living and one very much not.\
 n\nFilled with sharp dialogue\, clever humor\, and delightfully chaotic si
 tuations\, *Blithe Spirit* is a timeless comedy that proves some relations
 hips are difficult to leave behind\, even after death.\n\nMeet the Cast\n\
 n**Flint Berberich** as Charles Condomine\n\n**Jade Stanton** as Ruth Cond
 omine\n\n**Devyn Lawrence-Hall** as Elvira Condomine\n\n**Bella Lessig** a
 s Madame Arcati\n\n**Giselle De Leon** as Dr. George Bradman\n\n**Catania 
 DeKeyrel** as Mrs. Violet Bradman\n\n**Cailey Gettle and Amiya Clark** as 
 Edith\n\nPerformance Dates & Times\n\nJoin us for one of four performances
 :\n\n**Thursday\, November 12** — 7:00 PM\n\n**Friday\, November 13** 
 — 7:00 PM\n\n**Sunday\, November 15** — 2:00 PM\n\n**Monday\, November
  16** — 7:00 PM\n\n**Location:** Emily Gates Performing Arts Center\, Sa
 n Marin High School\, Novato\, CA\n\n**Co-Directed by Brad Smith and Linda
  Kislingbury**\n\nTickets & Admission\n\n**General Admission: $5 Students 
 / $10 Adults** General seating / Opening Seating. No reserved seats.\n\nTi
 ckets will be available for purchase at the door beginning one hour before
  each performance. Come enjoy an entertaining evening (or afternoon!) of l
 ive theater while supporting the talented student actors and crew who brin
 g this spirited comedy to the stage. We look forward to seeing you there!
LOCATION:Emily Gates Performing Arts Center - San Marin High
URL:https://www.sanmarinperformingarts.org/news-highlights/blithe-spirit
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
