BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CNPS Speaker Series - Author of Indigenous cooking/culture book
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T210000
UID:261104qLTgIYZn2kW1UE3rIDMoow
DESCRIPTION:Sara Calvosa Olson \\(Karuk\\) is the author of Chími Nu’am
 : Native California Foodways for the Contemporary Kitchen \\(Heyday\, 2023
 \\). Her work dwells at the intersection of storytelling\, Indigenous food
  systems\, traditional phenological knowledge\, and community food securit
 y. With an interest in using both culturally sound and faithfully updated 
 techniques that honor traditional plants and animals\, her cooking inspire
 s a new look at California's oldest foods.\n\nJoin Sara in conversation ab
 out the past\, present\, and future of food sovereignty\, and how we can d
 evelop deeper understandings of climate issues by centering Indigenous rem
 atriation efforts.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Art and Garden Center
URL:https://chapters.cnps.org/milobaker/2026/10/27/november-17-speaker-ser
 ies-sara-calvosa-olson-karuk/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
