BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wreckless Strangers at Rancho Nicasio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
UID:2611063F9EPbhFdEaub87tpnw1Xg
DESCRIPTION:Riding high from their recent performance at Hardly Strictly 
 Bluegrass\, Ameri-Cali Soul band Wreckless Strangers are kicking off the
  holiday season with their first Christmas song\, “Christmas Tears\,”
  arriving November 6. The band will debut the single live\, alongside its
  signature blend of originals and crowd-pleasing covers\, at Rancho Nicas
 io on Friday\, November 20\, followed by a show at Lucca Bar & Grill in
  Benicia on Saturday\, December 19.\n\nThe two performances bring Wreckl
 ess Strangers’ soulful\, roots-driven rock to two special corners of the
  Bay Area. On November 20\, the band takes the stage at Rancho Nicasio\, 
 the historic West Marin roadhouse known for live music\, dinner shows\, an
 d its laid-back country setting. On December 19\, they perform at Lucca B
 ar & Grill in Benicia\, a waterfront town with a welcoming small-town fee
 l and a lively dining and music scene.\n\nOriginally released by Sonny Th
 ompson and Robert Wilson and made famous by blues legend Freddie King\, 
 “Christmas Tears” takes on new life through Wreckless Strangers’ sou
 l-driven arrangement\, old-school piano\, and emotionally charged vocals.\
 n\nRecorded at the legendary FAME Recording Studios in Muscle Shoals\, Al
 abama\, the single offers a different perspective on the season. Rather th
 an focusing on the usual joy and nostalgia\, the band leans into a more me
 lancholy side of the holidays\, with lead vocalist Amber Morris deliveri
 ng a standout performance that balances technical precision with the song
 ’s raw emotion.\n\nThe idea for the band’s first Christmas release had
  been circulating for years. In April\, while visiting Tennessee\, the ban
 d found a break between shows in Nashville and Knoxville and seized the op
 portunity to record at FAME Studios with producer David Kalmusky\, whose
  credits include Keith Urban\, Carrie Underwood\, Justin Bieber\, and Jour
 ney. It was Amber who suggested “Christmas Tears\,” an unconventional 
 choice that proved to be the perfect fit.\n\n“Christmas Tears” will be
  available on all streaming platforms on November 6.
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:http://ranchonicasio.com/events/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Olio Nuovo Harvest and Milling Experience at Gold Ridge Organic Fa
 rms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T141500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T153000
UID:261104xfYr11F750GGbR4uQDg0CA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable behind-the-scenes journey into th
 e heart of our olive harvest season. This experience offers a rare opportu
 nity to see how our award-winning olive oil is crafted\, from the branches
  of our olive trees to the first drops of the season’s oil.\n\nYour jour
 ney begins with a guided tour of our 88-acre organic farm. You’ll step i
 nto the orchards to watch our expert team harvest fresh olives straight fr
 om the trees at their peak of flavor.\n\nNext\, you’ll visit our state-o
 f-the-art olive oil mill\, where you’ll learn about the milling process 
 and see the olives pressed into vibrant\, fresh Olio Nuovo\, the celebrate
 d “new oil” prized by culinary enthusiasts for its brilliant green hue
  and robust\, peppery finish.\n\nThe highlight comes right at the source: 
 tasting fresh Olio Nuovo straight from the mill just moments after the oli
 ves are crushed.\n\nBook now to secure your spot for this rare\, behind-th
 e-scenes look at our harvest traditions.\n\nImportant Notes: Please wear c
 omfortable shoes suitable for walking on a working farm This outdoor exper
 ience may be canceled due to wet weather. Full refund available.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/627571/olio
 -nuovo-harvest-and-milling-experience
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Threads of Thunder Indigenous Fashion Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T200000
UID:261103dWaiPNVxf0ic9UfBjfufkA
DESCRIPTION:INDIGENOUS FASHION TAKES CENTER STAGE IN SANTA ROSA\n\n**SANTA
  ROSA\, CA —** Finest Feathers proudly presents the **4th Annual Threads
  of Thunder Indigenous Fashion Show** on **Friday\, November 20\, 2026**\,
  at the **Sonoma County Fairgrounds – Finley Hall**.\n\nThis powerful ev
 ening will bring Indigenous creativity to the runway through **Native desi
 gners\, models\, artists\, vendors\, and live entertainment** — all whil
 e celebrating culture\, community\, entrepreneurship\, and the next genera
 tion of Indigenous talent.\n\nMore than a fashion show\, **Threads of Thun
 der is a celebration of Indigenous excellence** and an opportunity for the
  community to come together\, support Native creatives\, and experience co
 ntemporary Indigenous fashion in Northern California.\n\n**Doors Open: 4:0
 0 PM for Vendor Market | Show: 5:00–8:00 PM** **Sonoma County Fairground
 s – Finley Hall | Santa Rosa\, CA**\n\n**Tickets are on sale now at Fine
 stFeathers.com**\n\n**THREADS OF THUNDER — Where Culture Meets the Runwa
 y.**
LOCATION: Sonoma County Fair Grounds (Finley Hall) 
URL:http://www.finestfeathers.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AURORA SINGH headlines Friday Night Comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T220000
UID:261103XaYvBV1k8k-pWKNtinPymQ
DESCRIPTION:Friday night stand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa with Auror
 a Singh\n\nStand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nVIP TABLES NOW AVAILA
 BLE! Snag a table for 4 with preferred seating\, your own private call but
 ton to summon service\, and your first round of beer/cider (or a bottle of
  wine) for only $95! Every Friday night hilarious comedians from The Bay A
 rea and beyond perform at Barrel Proof Lounge. Stick around after for late
 -night karaoke!\n\nFresh lineup of funny each Friday.\n\nThis Week: Host: 
 Josh Argyle Noah Radke Drew Shafer\n\nHeadliner: Aurora Singh\n\nSome call
  her a rare breed\, I would agree. Aurora Singh blessed her immigrant pare
 nts with her arrival into the world in January 1992 and continuously douse
 d her sparkle upon the world as she grew up in Sacramento\, California in 
 the good ol’ Catholic school system. You won’t regret the deep belly l
 aughs you experience as a result of her hilarious straight forward real co
 medy. After 9 years of bringing the funny\, Aurora has been featured on Si
 rius XM\, ABC’s The 100K Pyramid and has performed with incredible comed
 ians such as Sheng Wang\, Greg Fitzsimons\, Anthony Jeselnik\, Roy Wood Jr
 . and Hasan Minhaj. She has also entered the college and cruise markets no
 w taking her reach nationally! Her mom has even been quoted saying\, “sh
 e’s hilarious!” Ready to ride the giggle train? All aboard! -Recurring
  feature at Laughs Unlimited Comedy Club in Sacramento\, CA. -Recurring Li
 ve Nation host: hosts at San Francisco Punch Line\, Sacramento Punch Line\
 , and Cobb's Comedy Club. -Recurring feature at Loonee’s Comedy Corner\,
  Colorado Springs\, CO. -Recurring host at Rooster T. Feathers Comedy Club
 \, Sunnyvale\, CA. -Recurring feature act for Mic Drop Comedy Club San Die
 go. -Headliner Laughingstock Comedy Club\, Bakersfield\, CA. -Showcase pro
 ducer with Live Nation at the Sacramento Punch Line. -Showcase producer at
  Sacramento Comedy Spot. -Accepted into Women in Comedy Festival 2020. -Wo
 rld Series of Comedy Semi-Finalist 2020. -Big Pine Comedy Festival “Best
  of Fest” award 2022. -Made virtual Chocolate Sundaes history by getting
  100% of the audience vote to move to the live show at the Hollywood Laugh
  Factory 2022. -Sac Town Comedy Get Down Festival “Best of Fest” 2022.
  -World Series of Comedy Semi-Finalist 2022 -World Series of Comedy Laughs
  Unlimited Semi-Finalist 2023 -Season 6 Episode 15 of the 100K Pyramid on 
 ABC and Hulu -APCA Comedian of the Year 2025 -Regular headlining act on No
 rwegian Cruise Lines Check out her website at **https://www.aurorasinghcom
 edy.com/**\n\n21+ Doors - 7p / Show - 8p $15adv / $20door\n\nCheck out **w
 ww.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/aurora-singh-headlines-friday-night-comed
 y-in-downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-2001405654188?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
