DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
UID:261031sRI2R3Ya70O0QfOUgJ5G6g
DESCRIPTION:**C Major Moods**\n\nJoint Concert featuring the Sonoma State 
 Symphony Orchestra (Alexander Kahn\, Music Director) and the Santa Rosa Sy
 mphony Young People's Chamber Orchestra(Aaron Westman\, Music Director)\n\
 nPlease join us for an evening of two remarkable symphonies from the early
  nineteenth century\, both of which are in the key of C!\n\nThis concert i
 s a collaboration between the Sonoma State Symphony Orchestra and the Sant
 a Rosa Symphony Young People's Chamber Orchestra\, who will join forces th
 roughout the program.\n\nOn the first half of the program is the passionat
 e and virtuousic Symphony no. 1 from 1847 by Emile Mayer\, the most prolif
 ic female composer active in Germany during the 19th century. After the in
 termission we bring you Beethoven's ground-breaking Symphony No. 1 (1800)\
 , the symphony that launched the Romantic period and put Beethoven's name 
 on the map as a symphonist. The Beethoven will be performed without a cond
 uctor\, led from the violin by SSU violin/viola faculty member and YPCO Mu
 sic Director Aaron Westman.
LOCATION:Green Music Center - Weill Hall
URL:https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-2?utm_source=sonoma
 _calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orche
 stra_nov20
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
