BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holiday Boutique
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T140000
UID:261113drJU8y29QEa5SakHquO9Lg
DESCRIPTION:St. Paul's Holiday Boutique is almost here! The sparkling even
 t that takes place annually the Saturday before Thanksgiving begins at 10 
 a.m. Saturday\, Nov. 21 at the St. Paul's Episcopal Church parish hall\, 2
 09 Matheson St. in Healdsburg. We offer items to streamline your holiday p
 reparation and gift-giving\, and who can't use a helping hand during this 
 jam-packed season. Look for our wide assortment of jams\, jellies\, marmal
 ade\, preserves\, chutneys and candies\; and baked goods of all kinds incl
 uding cookies\, pies and breads that can be served now or frozen for later
 . Pick up jars of bean-soup mix to simmer and serve a crowd\; and a favori
 te for gifting: cookie mixes that are prettily packaged\; just add your ow
 n egg and butter\, stir up and bake for a one-bowl batch of homemade cooki
 es in a flash. And there are plenty of other items to make your holidays b
 righter: We offer a wide selection of lovely costume jewelry along with ho
 liday decorations\, housewares\, serving pieces\, linens and toys. Stop by
  and see! Nearby parking is free.
LOCATION:St. Paul's Episcopal Church parish hall
URL:http://www.stpauls-healdsburg.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers 2026 Holiday Book & Craft Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T133000
UID:261112Z28Y7bHbY0Wc73bWB7g6xw
DESCRIPTION:**Redwood Writers 2026 Holiday Book & Craft Fair**\n\n**Novemb
 er 21\, 2026\, 11 a.m. Finley Center in Santa Rosa FREE!**\n\nJoin us on S
 aturday\, November 21\, from 11 a.m. to 1:30 p.m. in Room 5 (Senior Wing) 
 at the Finley Center for our 3rd Annual Holiday Party and Book & Craft Fai
 r! This lively\, event brings together local authors and crafters\, offeri
 ng books and handmade treasures that make perfect holiday gifts for yourse
 lf or your loved ones. Admission is FREE so that you can find the perfect 
 local gift for your loved ones. The afternoon will be a celebration among 
 friends\, delicious food\, and creative gifts made by local artisans and a
 uthors.\n\nMembers\, please bring a savory or sweet dish to share for our 
 potluck\, if you can!\n\nMark your calendars and plan to join us for a joy
 ful afternoon of shopping\, mingling\, and celebrating creativity in our c
 ommunity.\n\n**A chance to meet nice people with cool crafts\, books\, and
  other helpful services for creative souls and writers:**\n\n**Malena Elju
 maily** (Crafts): Knitted and crocheted items\, plus other handcrafts\n\n*
 *Taylor Metzler** (Books & Crafts): Books\, chainmaille jewelry\, crochete
 d items\n\n**Pamela Heck** (Books & Art)\n\n**Redwood Writers** (Books): R
 edwood Writers anthologies and swag\n\n**Patricia L. Morin** (Books): Psyc
 hological paranormal thriller *Moloch and the Angel*\; short story collect
 ions *Mystery Montage*\, *Crime Montage*\, *Confetti*\, *Deadly Illusions*
 \n\n**Stacey Dennick** (Other): Comic zines\, plus info on SRJC’s free L
 ifelong Learning classes\n\n**Crissi Langwell** (Books & Art): Romance boo
 ks and art\n\n**Shawn Langwell** (Books and Marketing Consulting): Persona
 l growth and inspirational books helping authors move past the mental obst
 acles of putting their work into the world\n\n**N.E. White** (Books): *Map
 maker* Books 1–3\; *The Legend of Damndrake* and *The Rescue of Damndrak
 e* (epic fantasy with dragons)\n\n**Janet Henker** (Books): Two novels and
  an anthology\, plus baked goods\n\n**Laura McHale Holland** (Books): Nove
 ls\, short story collections\, memoirs\n\n**Sarah Paris** (Books): Haiku a
 nd magic realism novellas\n\n**Natalie Gould** (Books): Memoir\, plus craf
 ts (dried flower wreaths\, paintings\, cards)\n\n**Lisa Manterfield** (Boo
 ks): Mystery/suspense novels *A Strange Companion*\, *The Smallest Thing*\
 , *All Our Lies Are True*\n\n**Dawn Dolan** (Books): Two children’s book
 s with matching merch (mugs\, thermoses\, plushies)\n\n**Ken Berman** (Boo
 ks): Books\, magnets\, and character merch\n\n**Brian Martens** (Books & A
 rt): Poetry books *Three Raven Gate* and *Merlin’s Wing*\, plus small pa
 intings\n\n**Neil Burgstahler** (Books)\n\n**Joan Tabb** (Books)\n\n**Tess
 a Burns** (Books)
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/redwood-writers-2026-holiday-book-craft-fai
 r/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kokedama - Living Plant Arrangement Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T160000
UID:261112TfmcZQdxjkGFPxx9ilAymQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a hands-on journey into the Japanese art of kokeda
 ma-living plant arrangements wrapped in moss. In this workshop\, you'll le
 arn the traditional techniques of forming and binding moss balls\, while e
 xploring the balance of beauty\, simplicity\, and nature that defines this
  practice. Guided by Cathrina of Cat Hawk Gardens—The Kokedama Mama—yo
 u’ll create your own kokedamas to take home\, along with the skills to c
 ontinue making more on your own. No prior experience is needed\; just brin
 g curiosity and a love of plants.\n\nThis workshop also includes a gentle\
 , grounding Self-Breema movement practice to help you connect body and min
 d before diving into your creative work. \n\n$150 per person\, includes i
 nstruction\, care and supplies for making two Kokedamas.\n\nSpace is limit
 ed. Registration closes on Friday\, 11.20 at 2pm or when full.
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Write Now! with Mark Sanford Gross
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T170000
UID:261112K7uh7EEWGUmAg2iFx2LRoA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for *Write Now!*\, a new writing group led by local wr
 iting coach Mark Sanford Gross. \n\n*Write Now!* is an in-the-moment prog
 ram for all folks who want to explore free writing\, story-telling\, and c
 uriosity about what happens when you get a notebook\, pen\, and a nudge. S
 hare the beauty of 'the spoken word' with others in this enthusiastic comm
 unity-building event through writing in a non-judgemental and trusting atm
 osphere. Bring friends and family.\n\nMark Sanford Gross has been building
  community through writing for the past few years along our coast.  He is
  the Creator and Co-Host of the local radio station's weekly program KGUA-
 Writers. He hosts writing workshops for local schools\, recovery programs 
 at Mendonoma Health Alliance\, and local pop-up destinations.
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comedian Don Friesen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T203000
UID:2611126m-t7d0jkEyswxzP5LOQWQ
DESCRIPTION:The Laugh Cellar presents: \n\nLos Angeles-based Don Friesen 
 is an award-winning headliner comedian known for his high-energy\, physica
 l\, and sharply relatable comedy. The only two-time winner in the 50-year 
 history of the San Francisco Comedy Competition\, Friesen has appeared on 
 Showtime\, Netflix\, Amazon Prime\, Comedy Central\, Dry Bar Comedy\, and 
 SiriusXM. Friesen blends observational comedy\, storytelling\, improvisati
 on\, and physicality into a style all his own. His latest special\, *Break
  a Leg*\, finds Friesen older\, possibly wiser\, and—spoiler alert—not
  quite as married as he used to be. Whether navigating technology\, relati
 onships\, or the absurdities of everyday life\, Friesen has a knack for tu
 rning real-life chaos into big laughs.\n\nIndoor Event - Balletto Vineyard
 s Reserve Room\n\nTheater style seating\n\nWine by the bottle and savory s
 nacks available for purchase. \n\n21+ \n\nDoors 6:00 PM
LOCATION:Balletto Vineyards
URL:https://www.crushersofcomedy.com/november212026.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Personalized Holiday Ornament Workshop at Made Local
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T130000
UID:261111wAXbWGvR30qrh7WSslAtGw
DESCRIPTION:Join local artist Irina Miller for a festive\, family-friendly
  workshop creating your own personalized holiday ornaments using acrylic p
 aint and mixed-media techniques.\n\nIrina will guide you step-by-step as y
 ou design and decorate 2–3 unique ornaments. Personalize them with names
 \, words\, messages\, or your own creative touches—perfect for hanging o
 n your tree or giving as handmade holiday gifts.\n\nNo painting experience
  is necessary\, and all materials are included.\n\nIn this workshop\, you 
 will:\n\n• Create 2–3 personalized holiday ornaments\n\n• Explore ac
 rylic painting and mixed-media techniques\n\n• Add names\, words\, or ot
 her personal details to your designs\n\n• Leave with handmade ornaments 
 ready for the holiday season\n\nDetails:\n\n• $45 per person\n\n• Ages
  7+\n\n• 2 hours\n\n• All materials included\n\n• No experience nece
 ssary\n\nImportant Notes:\n\n• Advance registration required • Worksho
 ps require a minimum of 4 participants • 72 hours notice required for a 
 partial refund • Workshop held outdoors under cover at Made Local Market
 place in Montgomery Village
LOCATION:Made Local
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/personalized-holiday-ornament-wo
 rkshop-at-made-local/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Night of the Troubadours at the Art & Music Gallery in Petaluma
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T210000
UID:261111d8F4_mmhH0SPU6KficoFXA
DESCRIPTION:Take a break from holiday stress and relax to the acoustic sou
 nds of Randy and the Special Agents\, Andrew Maurer\, and Bobby Bradford. 
 Originals and classics all in one night! Pizza and beverages while supplie
 s last. FREE\, and all donations benefit COTS of Petaluma.\n\nRandy and th
 e Special Agents has been playing since 2009. Our new acoustic version has
  Steve Roraus on bass\, Nick Bondoc and Burjor Dastur on guitar\, Sal More
 no on harmonica\, and Ann Moreno\, vocals. Blues standards\, country\, cur
 rent\, and a bit of rock are in the mix.\n\nAndrew Maurer has been writing
  songs and playing instruments for 30 years.   Drawing inspiration from 
 US folk traditional music and songwriters such as Kate Wolf\, Elliot Smith
 \, and Mississippi John Hurt\, he crafts his own style and regularly plays
  live at wine bars.  His 2025 EP called *When the Sadness Subsides* can b
 e found on all streaming platforms.\n\n"Professor Bad Bobby" Bradford has 
 had scads of plays produced\, stories and poems published\, songs recorded
 \, and gigs performed. Considering his varied and vivid life experiences\,
  he's not likely to run out of material any time soon.\n\nYou don’t want
  to miss it! Enjoy great music\, and benefit COTS of Petaluma. Grab a frie
 nd\, and come dance!
LOCATION:Art and Music Gallery
URL:https://artandmusicgallery.com/upcoming-events/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
