BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T220000
UID:261108O-fxZ_azj0-C8ovwHk4dAQ
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\nTrigger warnings: Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in Yid
 dish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Mayflower: An Interesting Mix of Passengers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T143000
UID:261108I-RoyZ_6IEqCPegYyc0M8w
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society Presents\n\n **The Mayf
 lower: An Interesting Mix of Passengers**\n\n **Presented by Suzanne Braye
 r**\n\n In 1620\, an English merchant ship\, The Mayflower\, left Southamp
 ton England for the New World carrying 102 men\, women\, children and a cr
 ew of 30. What motivated them to embark on this incredibly dangerous journ
 ey into the unknown? In addition to the passengers\; the ship\, the journe
 y\, The Mayflower Compact\, the early history of the Plymouth Colony and t
 he ubiquitous myths\, these all make for fascinating stories.\n\n Ms. Bra
 yer has a BA from Indiana University and a MA in history and education fro
 m Arizona State University. She enjoyed a career in secondary education fo
 r 30 years. After retirement\, she became a professional genealogist. She 
 is a past president of The Family History Society of Arizona\, a member of
  West Valley Genealogy Society\, The Arizona Genealogy Advisory Board\, an
 d numerous county societies in Indiana and North Carolina. She has taught 
 genealogy classes and spoken to numerous groups throughout Arizona and the
  West.\n\n Saturday\, November 21st\n\n Meeting starts at 12:30 pm\, pre
 sentation starts at 1:00 pm PST\n\n Meeting Details : The meeting is held
  via Zoom. Login begins at 12:30 p.m.\n\n FREE Via ZOOM\n\n Register at
  **https://www.scgsonline.org**\n\n Registration closes Friday\,  Novemb
 er 20th
URL:https://www.scgsonline.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music with Doron & Friends
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T210000
UID:261107TU96lBHx0EeQw9_TdejMHw
DESCRIPTION:Retro-funky-folk-rockers Doron & Friends cover the 60's & 70's
  songs you love!\n\nGet ready for a night of live music\, free popcorn\, a
 nd good vibes!\n\nDoron and Friends is an ever-evolving musical project of
  Sonoma County mid-life retro-funky-folk-rocker Doron Amiran. Doron’s or
 iginal songs celebrate life\, love\, and music\, drawing inspiration from 
 all the killer bands he grew up listening to in the ’60s & ’70s. Doron
  and Friends’ shows blend those songs with an eclectic array of covers\,
  some that you probably know\, and some that you probably don’t! Check o
 ut their album Making Music on all the streaming channels\, and boogie dow
 n at the show! Come happy\, leave happier!\n\nLive music at 6PM Barrel Pro
 of Lounge\, Downtown Santa Rosa Free entry • 21+ • Good times guarante
 ed.\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times
  ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://DoronandFriends.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stone Wrapping Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T150000
UID:261106pX_D7msS20-X_SbajIZq1Q
DESCRIPTION:In this class\, students will be creating decorative stones\, 
 utilizing wrapping techniques that can be applied outside of this class. S
 tudents will learn 3 basic knots with time allotted between each lesson fo
 r students to experiment creating new stones with the new knot. This appro
 ach allows everyone’s imagination to run wild\, fostering creativity and
  allowing time for new ideas.\n\nAll materials provided.\n\nStudents often
  make 6-8 stones per class.\n\nThere will be discussion breaks\, and a lun
 ch break throughout the class. Please bring water and a paper bag lunch.\n
 \nAbout the Teacher: Carrie Botto is a self taught multi-medium weaver. Sh
 e started weaving with beads over 40 years ago and continues to add skills
  and techniques to her “tool box”. Carrie travels all over the country
  now teaching several different classes\, and has taught at Mendocino Art 
 Center\, New Mexico Bead Trader\, Moab Art Center\, and Fiber on 4th in Ne
 w Mexico. Follow Carrie on Instagram @beanstreetsudio!
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/stone-wrapping
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music at Spicy Vines by The Ramblers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T180000
UID:261106i179GUCaf0SBEVQqBMcwjg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for live music in our tasting room! Reserve your spot 
 for this Saturday Live Music & Tasting Experience\, where exceptional wine
 s\, laid-back vibes\, and great live music come together for an unforgetta
 ble afternoon.\n\nFeatured Band\n\nThe Ramblers The Ramblers bring an unmi
 stakable fusion of Americana\, classic rock ’n’ roll\, and roots-inspi
 red country to every performance. Their sound is rich with acoustic textur
 es\, heartfelt harmonies\, and the kind of rhythm that draws listeners in 
 from the first note. Blending timeless influences with their own spirited 
 flair\, Jason Uber and Dave McClary create a live experience that’s both
  intimate and electric — a true celebration of connection\, melody\, and
  the joy of good music shared.\n\nDetails\n\nWalk-ins are welcome\, but pr
 iority seating is given to wine club members and guests with reservations.
  This event tends to fill up quickly\, so we highly recommend making a res
 ervation to secure your table. No outside food is allowed\, but we are dog
  and family friendly. For large groups of 13 or more\, please email us at 
 visit@spicyvines.com.
LOCATION:Spicy Vines Winery
URL:https://spicyvines.com/events/saturday-live-music-tasting/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
