DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T190000
UID:261104b2hTK08siUGxiyfjlvJrUw
DESCRIPTION:Two bands\, one amazing night in Petaluma's best club.\n\nGet 
 ready for an evening of irresistible grooves\, global rhythms\, and seriou
 s soul!\n\nOpening the night\, **SOUL MOSAIC** brings its unique World Gro
 ove sound to the stage\, blending original music with influences from Afri
 can\, Caribbean\, Jazz\, Funk\, Latin\, and beyond. Featuring **Rasaki Ala
 dokun of the King Sunny Adé Band on talking drum**\, Soul Mosaic delivers
  a deep rhythmic experience. Driving percussion\, intricate guitar work\, 
 soulful melodies\, and dynamic horn lines come together in a sound that wi
 ll feed your soul and move your body.\n\nThen keep the party going with Pe
 taluma's own **THE COZYCATS!** Bringing a killer mix of classic favorites 
 from Joss Stone to Curtis Mayfield alongside a collection of fresh origina
 ls\, The Cozycats have something for everyone. With a stage full of funkif
 ied horns\, keyboards\, percussion\, and the smoking lead vocals of the on
 e and only Kozue Ikusaki\, these cats keep the dancefloor jumping.
LOCATION:The Big Easy
URL:https://bigeasypetaluma.com/events/cozycats
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:David Dondero Music & Virgil Shaw
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T200000
UID:261103mwdkj5ROJEeaTBuT4276ug
DESCRIPTION:David Dondero\, an American troubadour\, was born in Duluth\, 
 Minnesota in 1969. His love of music began with folk rock and country of t
 he early 70’s and evolved to include punk rock and hip hop of the 80’s
 . He spent his formative years in suburban Chicago and northern New Jersey
  listening to pirate radio and heavy metal. As a young man\, music molded 
 Dondero’s life. \n\nDondero began writing songs in the late 80’s while
  at Clemson. Initially a drummer and lyricist\, he formed Sunbrain in 1991
 . A post-punk indie rock quartet heavily influenced by Donovan and Fugazi.
  Sunbrain was signed by Grass Records and they recorded 3 albums. When the
  group disbanded he went on to play drums for the folk punk band\, This Bi
 ke is a Pipe Bomb. After 2 years he left the band and began his solo caree
 r. He’s been touring for thirty years and his music has taken him around
  the world multiple times.\n\nHis style and ongoing narratives are hard to
  fit into a particular genre. The music is inspired by heartbreak\, hopefu
 lness\, everyday work and his never ending tour of life.  Dondero’s lyri
 cs are influenced by the angst of Black Flag\, the wanderlust of Bruce Spr
 ingsteen\, the sentimentality of Paul Simon and the politics of Woody Guth
 rie. \n\nHe’s shared bills and tours with Pedro the Lion\, The Mountain 
 Goats\, Darren Hanlon\, Daniel Johnston and Against Me! In 2006 Bob Boilen
  and Robin Hilton of NPR put David on their list of the top ten greatest l
 iving songwriters. Aside from multiple years at South by Southwest\, he wa
 s invited by Mudhoney as a featured artist at All Tomorrow’s Parties in 
 Rye\, England. God Speed You Black Emperor brought him to The Sled Island 
 Festival in Calgary. And he played the Bellow Winter Music Festival in Aus
 tralia under the recommendation of Australian songwriter Darren Hanlon. \n
 \nHe has split seven inches with Mischief Brew and the Pine Hill Haints. D
 ondero has recorded ten albums and his 11th is slated to come out on Fluff
  and Gravy Records in Summer of 2023. Recorded in Portland at Fluff and Gr
 avy Studio. Dondero calls Portland\, Santa Cruz and Pensacola home and is 
 about to publish his first novel. \n\n\\*Follow links to these indie label
 s to see Dondero's upcoming & past releases:\n\nFluff and Gravy Records: h
 ttps://fluffandgravy.com/\n\nGhostmeat Records:  www.ghostmeat.com\n\nKeel
 ed Scales:  www.keeledscales.com\n\nTeam Love Records: https://www.discogs
 .com/label/74630-Team-Love-Records\n\nFlippin' Yeah Records \\(Australia\\
 ): https://flippinyeahindustries.bigcartel.com/products\n\nTotal Treble:  
 https://www.discogs.com/release/11706850-David-Dondero-W-Love
LOCATION:The Elephant In the Room
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109093051?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
