UID:260929fbRl854-TUqH1RmZ5wqyRw
DESCRIPTION:SUNDAY SESSIONS IN THE LOUNGE ROTATING DJs • OPEN FORMAT •
  REQUESTS WELCOME • NO COVER\n\nSunday nights have a new home in The Lou
 nge at Barrel Proof.\n\nEvery Sunday at 8 PM\, a rotating lineup of DJs ta
 kes over the front room for Sunday Sessions — an open-format dance party
  where the playlist isn't locked into one genre and requests are part of t
 he fun.\n\nOpen format means the DJ gets to read the room. One song might 
 take you back\, the next might be something you were blasting in the car t
 his week. Different genres\, different eras and different DJs from week to
  week\, with plenty of room for the crowd to help steer the night.\n\nGot 
 a song you want to hear? Ask the DJ.\n\nAnd there's more happening under t
 he same roof. Start your evening with Sunday Funday Comedy at 6 PM\, then 
 at 8 PM Barrel Proof gives you two ways to keep the night going:\n\n THE 
 LOUNGE — 8 PM Sunday Sessions Rotating DJs • Open Format • Requests 
 • Dancing\n\n MAIN ROOM — 8 PM Sunday Night Karaoke Grab the mic and 
 sing on the big stage.\n\nDance in the Lounge\, sing in the Main Room\, or
  bounce between the two all night.\n\nEvery Sunday • 8 PM Barrel Proof L
 ounge 501 Mendocino Ave • Downtown Santa Rosa 21+ • No Cover\n\nCheck 
 out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/sunday-sessions-in-the-lounge-djs-dancing
 -requests-tickets-2002178174818?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lucy Kaplansky
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T180000
UID:260910tDj85AOxsUmmYjmbKJ9C6A
DESCRIPTION:Lucy Kaplansky \\(born 1960\\) is a folk musician based in New
  York City. \n\n Originally from Chicago\, at the age of 18\, moved to New
  York City where she became involved in the city's Greenwich Village folk 
 music scene.\n\n \n\n In 1983\, she decided to become a psychologist\, enr
 olling in Yeshiva University. She continued playing music while doing her 
 PhD\, and began to have some success as part of a duo with Shawn Colvin. H
 owever\, when they began to attract record company interest\, Kaplansky de
 clined\, choosing instead to set up a private practice and become a staff 
 psychologist at a New York hospital. For several years\, she concentrated 
 largely on her work\, and played little in the way of concerts. However\, 
 she still did some session work\, such as singing backing vocals in the st
 udio for Suzanne Vega.\n\n \n\n By the early 1990s she found herself incre
 asingly drawn back to music. Colvin\, who by this time had experienced som
 e commercial success\, offered to produce an album for her. The result\, T
 he Tide\, a mixture of her own songs and several covers\, was released by 
 Red House Records \\(Greg Brown's label\\) in 1994. At this time\, she dec
 ided to give up her psychology practice\, and return to music full-time. S
 he released her second album\, \\[album artist=Lucy Kaplansky\\]Flesh and 
 Bone\, in 1996.\n\n \n\n In 1998 Kaplansky joined with Dar Williams and Ri
 chard Shindell to form the folk group Cry Cry Cry\, which made an album an
 d toured extensively resulting from the success of the originally planned 
 six week tour. \n\n \n\n 1999's Ten Year Night won rave reviews and booste
 d her popularity\, leading to performances on CBS-TV. \n\n She followed th
 at album with Every Single Day which was released in 2001.\n\n \n\n The Re
 d Thread\, released in early 2004\, includes songs about adopting her new 
 daughter Molly\, who Lucy and her husband Rick brought home from China in 
 late 2003\, and several songs relating to her experiences living in downto
 wn Manhattan during 9-11. A new album is to be released in March of 2007.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108207770?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
