BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tower of Power
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T200000
UID:260801yqzt-nbZxEaqiQ6U0ur0UQ
DESCRIPTION:Relive the 70s when Tower of Power returns to the LBC on Satur
 day\, November 28! For 58 years\, Tower of Power has delivered the best in
  funk and soul music. Once East Bay Grease defined their sound\, the 70s w
 ere a boom period for the band with radio classics like “So Very Hard to
  Go” and “What Is Hip?” They continued to tour and record over the y
 ears\, returning to Oakland in 2018 for their 50th anniversary. They’ve 
 travelled the world\, enjoying hit singles on their own and backing legend
 ary artists\, including Otis Redding\, Elton John\, Santana\, the Grateful
  Dead\, John Lee Hooker\, Aerosmith\, Bonnie Raitt\, and countless others.
  In the process they’ve defined the instantly recognizable “Oakland so
 ul” sound.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/tower-of-power-26/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T170000
UID:261004R4aLy2FoDkyzbxKwT5zvlA
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Happy Hour - The Ukulele Ramblers - Open Uke Jam!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T180000
UID:2611140FGHR56Rokm-h5-9yyPqdQ
DESCRIPTION:Saturday afternoons hit differently at Barrel Proof Lounge.\n\
 nWe open early — 3pm — and hand the room over to Ukulele Ramblers\, a 
 friendly\, talented ukulele collective that turns Happy Hour into a laid-b
 ack\, sing-along hang.\n\nThis is live music and an open uke jam. Bring yo
 ur ukulele if you’ve got one. Bring your voice even if you don’t. The 
 Ramblers lead the way with familiar tunes\, easy harmonies\, and a welcomi
 ng vibe that makes it just as fun to join in as it is to sit back and list
 en.\n\nNo pressure. No ego. Just good songs\, good people\, and a room tha
 t feels like it belongs to everyone.\n\n Live Music & Open Uke Jam | 3–
 6pm  Happy Hour drinks  Free popcorn  21+\n\n Barrel Proof Lounge 501 
 Mendocino Avenue\, Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nIt’s the kind of afternoon you
  plan to stop by for one drink… and somehow stay for three hours.\n\n**w
 ww.UkuleleRamblers.net**\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for al
 l sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/live-music-happy-hour-the-ukulele-rambler
 s-open-uke-jam-tickets-1485589782029?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Weekend Santa Sightings
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T150000
UID:261110cjkwRYkYP02iUKVoO4cx6g
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the holidays and join us at the Village for photos w
 ith Santa happening on weekends from Saturday\, November 28th to Sunday\, 
 December 20th\, 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. daily.\n\nAppointments are highly recomm
 ended\, as we cannot guarantee that we can accommodate all walk-ups throug
 hout the event series. Reserve your 5-minute window now for a $35 fee duri
 ng our initial release (through Friday\, November 13). Beginning Saturday\
 , November 14\, the fee increases to $45. Each family will receive a print
  to take home that day\, as well as a digital copy of their photo followin
 g the appointment. Please note that we do not call or text waitlisted gues
 ts.\\*\n\nMake the most of your Santa visit:\n\nYour photo package include
 s up to five digital photos\, emailed the Monday following your appointmen
 t\, plus a print to take home that day.\n\nEnjoy writing letters to Santa 
 and dropping them off at the official Montgomery Village Santa Mail mailbo
 x\, plus crafts at our holiday craft tables.\n\nSweeten your visit! Stop b
 y Salt & Straw before or after your appointment and enjoy a complimentary 
 kids’ scoop with any ice cream purchase during Weekend Santa Sightings (
 valid each Saturday and Sunday from 11/28/26 to 12/20/26 between 11 a.m. t
 o 3 p.m.).\n\nKeep an eye out for ME SPA’s elves\, spreading holiday che
 er and a little stress relief with special cards to redeem at the spa. Bri
 ng yours in for a Chill Bag\, a holiday survival kit filled with goodies a
 nd coupons to help you keep your cool all season long. For an extra moment
  of relaxation\, enjoy a complimentary chair massage as scheduling allows.
 \n\nRetro Foto will be assisting in making this memory last a lifetime by 
 providing Santa with a vintage ride for all to enjoy! Retro Foto is Sonoma
  County’s boutique photo booth experience. Lola is a fully restored 1970
  Volkswagen bus that loves the camera – whether it’s as a photo booth 
 or a photo backdrop! Lola is all about making memories\, which is why Sant
 a thought this would be the perfect way to drive into the Holiday season!\
 n\nBy attending this event\, guests consent to appear in photo/video recor
 dings that may be used for website photography or other purposes.\n\n\\*A 
 portion of proceeds will benefit Sonoma County Secret Santa Program.
LOCATION:Montgomery Village - Courtyard
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/weekend-santa-sightings/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
