BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Very Merry Weekend
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T180000
UID:261110IqGjc3E1BUuqzlK_9tQm8w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for A Very Merry Weekend at Montgomery Village!\n\nCel
 ebrate the season with a weekend of exclusive retail offerings\, family-fr
 iendly entertainment\, festive trimmings at every turn\, and more.\n\nFrid
 ay\, November 27:\n\nLive holiday music from 12pm-2pm in The Courtyard\, c
 ourtesy of Jimmy Galvan.\n\nHoliday caroling from 3:30pm to 5:30pm across 
 property\, courtesy of Silver Belles Caroling Group.\n\nSaturday\, Novembe
 r 28:\n\nWeekend Santa Sightings begin! Photos with Santa take place in Th
 e Courtyard on weekends from Saturday\, November 28 to Sunday\, December 2
 0\, 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. daily. Appointments are highly recommended. A portio
 n of proceeds from Weekend Santa Sightings benefit Sonoma County Secret Sa
 nta Program. Book your spot here.\n\nCelebrate Small Business Saturday by 
 supporting local small businesses across the Village.\n\nCelebrate the sea
 son at our Second Annual Tree Lighting Celebration on Saturday\, November 
 28\, from 5–7 p.m. in The Courtyard!\n\nEnjoy a festive evening filled w
 ith holiday music\, creative activities\, and a special appearance by Sant
 a and Mrs. Claus. Admission is free\, with seasonal fun for the whole fami
 ly:\n\nLive holiday music and carolers\, plus a family-friendly holiday si
 ngalong at 6:45 p.m.\n\n\\- Complimentary hot cocoa\n\n\\- Churros and coo
 kies available for purchase\n\n\\- Complimentary caricature portraits\n\n\
 \- Custom wood-burned gift tags\n\n\\- Make-your-own mini snowmen and jing
 le bell wreath ornaments\n\n\\- Write your letters to Santa\, delivered th
 rough the official Montgomery Village Santa Mail mailbox\n\n\\- A special 
 visit from Santa and Mrs. Claus\n\n\\- Make the evening a little sweeter w
 ith a stop at Salt & Straw. During the event\, enjoy a complimentary scoop
  with the purchase of a scoop\, available November 28\, 2026\, from 5–7 
 p.m.\n\nSunday\, November 29:\n\nLive holiday music in The Courtyard\n\nAB
 OUT SONOMA COUNTY SECRET SANTA\n\nSonoma County’s Secret Santa is a nonp
 rofit gift-giving program\, providing gifts and holiday cheer to those les
 s fortunate in our community.\n\nSecret Santa has been bringing joy to peo
 ple throughout Sonoma County for over 30 years\, ensuring that children\, 
 teens\, adults\, and seniors who would not otherwise receive a holiday gif
 t have reason to celebrate and experience the compassion and generosity of
  their community.
LOCATION:Montgomery Village - Courtyard
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/a-very-merry-weekend-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T160000
UID:261108HArHre6LxUqsjZ9U3P-NuQ
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\nTrigger warnings: Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in Yid
 dish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rooted
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T163000
UID:26110697w2SwiKdUyk0oSN7xTUGg
DESCRIPTION:This holiday season\, Spreckels Theatre Company offers a heart
 warming alternative to traditional seasonal fare with *Rooted*\, a story a
 bout the messy\, fierce love that keeps us grounded. An intelligent\, gent
 le comedy by Deborah Zoe Laufer\, *Rooted* plays Nov. 27 – Dec.13!\n\nEm
 ery is perfectly content living in her beloved treehouse\, completely isol
 ated from the world\, communing with her plants. Meanwhile\, down on the g
 round\, her sister Hazel is thoroughly miserable\, slaving away at a dead-
 end diner job just to survive and financially support Emery’s eccentric 
 lifestyle. Looking on from the sidelines\, Luanne is yearning for somethin
 g\, anything to bring true meaning into her life.\n\n﻿The sisters' fragi
 le ecosystem is completely upended when Emery’s YouTube videos documenti
 ng her plant experiments unexpectedly go viral. Almost overnight\, her dig
 ital musings accidentally incite a full-blown CULT(!). As throngs of devot
 ed truth-seekers congregate below the treehouse\, the lives of all three w
 omen are plunged into chaos\, compelling each woman to choose their own pa
 th and find their bliss.\n\n*Pick-Your-Price Night: purchase sliding scale
  tickets starting at $10 each for the opening Friday night\, Nov. 27th.*
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts - Bette Condiotti Experi
 mental Theatre
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/rooted/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
