BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spencer LaJoye at Gather Petaluma - a Free\, Community Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T210000
UID:261109H_Bt4XFV4UGxH9AE5NaMMw
DESCRIPTION:Music for everyone: Our first concert is free!\n\nFree tickets
  required. Reserve yours at **www.gatherpetaluma.org**\n\nJoin us on Decem
 ber 4th as Spencer LaJoye takes the stage for Gather Petaluma’s first-ev
 er concert - free and open to all!\n\nMeet Spencer: Spencer LaJoye makes q
 ueer indie folk music for all. A coast-to-coast singer-songwriter and voca
 l loop artist with Midwest roots\, Spencer is a classically trained violin
 ist with a theater kid’s heart and a theology degree. They won the 2021 
 Kerrville Songwriting Competition and the 2024 Songwriter Serenade\, and t
 heir viral anthem “Plowshare Prayer” found a home in hearts around the
  world. Charming and full of banter\, Spencer will have you laughing one m
 oment and weeping the next.\n\nFriday\, December 4 · Doors 6:30 p.m. · M
 usic 7:00 p.m.\n\nInside the Sanctuary at Gather Petaluma\, 825 Middlefiel
 d Dr.\, Petaluma\n\nReserve your free ticket at **www.gatherpetaluma.org**
 \n\nWant to make the night extra special? Join our intimate pre-show recep
 tion with Spencer\, limited to just 12 guests. Your $100 ticket includes l
 ight refreshments\, a song performed only for reception guests and helps k
 eep the concert free for all. (Add it at checkout)\n\nFree tickets require
 d. Reserve yours at **www.gatherpetaluma.org**
LOCATION:Gather Petaluma
URL:http://www.gatherpetaluma.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T213000
UID:261108igr1YlIFC0q5Ehe4NAxPfQ
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\nTrigger warnings: Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in Yid
 dish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Amphibians of the San Francisco Bay Area Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T160000
UID:261106pfrvxVlSiEqFmqw7mA03Fw
DESCRIPTION:Join the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation for an in-depth works
 hop on the ecology\, identification\, life history\, and conservation of t
 he San Francisco Bay Area's 16 amphibian species.\n\nLed by amphibian expe
 rts Dave Cook and Jeff Alvarez\, this workshop is designed for professiona
 l biologists\, resource managers\, environmental consultants\, students\, 
 and others working with California wildlife. The workshop combines a full 
 day of classroom instruction with a small-group field trip to a private pr
 eserve in Sonoma County.\n\n The classroom presentation takes place Frida
 y\, December 4\, 2026\, from 8:30 am to 4:00 pm at the Laguna Environmenta
 l Center. Participants will also attend one field trip on Saturday\, Decem
 ber 5\, or Sunday\, December 6. Four identical sessions are available\, wi
 th morning and afternoon options each day.
LOCATION:Laguna Environmental Center
URL:https://2026amphibiansworkshop.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Merry & Bright
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T190000
UID:261106P9ccBZgd3EKzQJTNNxjGBw
DESCRIPTION:Step into Santa Rosa’s premier winter wonderland for the 6th
  Annual Merry & Bright!\n\nPresented by Sonoma Clean Power\, produced by t
 he Redwood Ice Theatre Company \\(RITC\\)\, and hosted at iconic Snoopy’
 s Home Ice\, this cherished holiday tradition returns with nine completely
  free outdoor ice skating shows. Gather the family to watch dazzling routi
 nes from professional skaters\, accompanied by classic holiday music and s
 easonal entertainment designed to bring neighbors together across Sonoma a
 nd Mendocino counties.\n\nIn the spirit of innovation and sustainability\,
  this year’s outdoor production is powered directly by Sonoma Clean Powe
 r’s all-electric Ford F-150 Lightning truck—showcasing clean energy in
  action while helping local households discover easy ways to save energy t
 his winter.\n\nAdmission: Completely free\, no tickets required!\n\nLocati
 on: Snoopy’s Home Ice\, Santa Rosa\n\nShow Schedule \\(9 Free Outdoor Pe
 rformances\\):\n\nFriday\, December 4: 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p.m.\n\nSaturday\,
  December 5: 2:00 p.m.\, 3:00 p.m.\, 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p.m.\n\nSunday\, Dec
 ember 6: 1:00 p.m.\, 2:00 p.m. & 3:00 p.m.\n\nPro Tip: Arrive early to bun
 dle up\, grab a hot cocoa\, and secure the best spot to watch the show!\n\
 nTo learn more about how SCP is giving back this holiday season\, visit: h
 ttps://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
LOCATION:Snoopy's Home Ice
URL:https://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rooted
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T220000
UID:261106OCpnmKmg4EOrtYXIqsAd8Q
DESCRIPTION:This holiday season\, Spreckels Theatre Company offers a heart
 warming alternative to traditional seasonal fare with *Rooted*\, a story a
 bout the messy\, fierce love that keeps us grounded. An intelligent\, gent
 le comedy by Deborah Zoe Laufer\, *Rooted* plays Nov. 27 – Dec.13!\n\nEm
 ery is perfectly content living in her beloved treehouse\, completely isol
 ated from the world\, communing with her plants. Meanwhile\, down on the g
 round\, her sister Hazel is thoroughly miserable\, slaving away at a dead-
 end diner job just to survive and financially support Emery’s eccentric 
 lifestyle. Looking on from the sidelines\, Luanne is yearning for somethin
 g\, anything to bring true meaning into her life.\n\n﻿The sisters' fragi
 le ecosystem is completely upended when Emery’s YouTube videos documenti
 ng her plant experiments unexpectedly go viral. Almost overnight\, her dig
 ital musings accidentally incite a full-blown CULT(!). As throngs of devot
 ed truth-seekers congregate below the treehouse\, the lives of all three w
 omen are plunged into chaos\, compelling each woman to choose their own pa
 th and find their bliss.\n\n*Pick-Your-Price Night: purchase sliding scale
  tickets starting at $10 each for the opening Friday night\, Nov. 27th.*
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts - Bette Condiotti Experi
 mental Theatre
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/rooted/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
