BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T170000
UID:260824kBiLJO3z10qSzft3ZEoZWA
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\n*Maple Magic* *& Winter Wonder* invites
  visitors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativ
 ity\, and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided wal
 ks\, hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by t
 he changing landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the 
 sweet fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experienc
 e the peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salsa Beginners 2 - Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T120000
UID:2604076vyLUjnxaU-FgTM_nMKp2w
DESCRIPTION:Ready to take your salsa to the next level? You’ve mastered 
 the basics\, now it’s time to add some flair and fluidity to your salsa 
 dancing.\n\nPre-requisite: Salsa Beginners 1 – You know your basic steps
 \, left turn\, right turn\, cross-body lead\, and you hold your frame.\n\n
 **What You’ll Learn**\n\nWe’ve curated a curriculum designed to build 
 your confidence and your “social dance” vocabulary:\n\n**• The Cross
  Body Lead (CBL) Series:** Master both **Inside and Outside Turns**\, the 
 essential building blocks for moving your partner across the floor with gr
 ace.\n\n**• The “I Turn – You Turn”:** A classic social dance stap
 le that develops timing and hand-change coordination.\n\n**• The Walk-Th
 rough:** Learn how to transition smoothly through the dance space without 
 breaking your rhythm.\n\n**• Footwork & Shine:** We’ll break down the 
 footwork pattern that adds personality to your “shines.”\n\n**Techniqu
 e & Artistry**\n\nDancing is about more than just where your feet go. In t
 his level\, we dive deeper into the “how”:\n\n**• The Frame:** Under
 stand the “tension and compression” needed to lead and follow clearly 
 without using muscle.\n\n**• Upper Body Mechanics:** Learn how to isolat
 e your ribcage and shoulders to move with that authentic Latin soul.\n\n**
 • Connection:** Developing a “heavy” but responsive arm connection t
 o ensure your partner feels every lead.\n\n**Important Details**\n\n**• 
 No dance experience required:** Whether you’ve never danced before or it
 ’s been a while\, you’re welcome here!\n\n**• No partner necessary:*
 * Come solo or bring a friend—either way\, you’ll have plenty of oppor
 tunities to dance.\n\n**•** Please wear **non-marking shoe soles:** This
  helps us keep our dance floor in great condition.\n\nDate & Time:\n\n**Th
 ursdays 7:30 PM**\n\n**Saturday 11:00 AM**\n\nInstructor: Lucie Ebnerova\n
 \nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway #8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minu
 tes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-beginners-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salsa Beginner Marin – Saturday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T110000
UID:260317VwnAbGwkk0aWk84pky8GFw
DESCRIPTION:**Ready to learn intermediate steps and technique?** Join on 
 on Saturday – Salsa Beginner Marin\n\nAre you a beginner who’s always 
 wanted to learn salsa? Salsa classes are designed to help you build a stro
 ng foundation. In this class\, you’ll learn the fundamental footwork\, p
 ractice the basic turns\, and understand the essential body movement that 
 will make you feel confident on the dance floor. This class is perfect for
  anyone ready to learn the techniques and foundational steps needed to sta
 rt their salsa journey.\n\nSalsa is fun\, and we make learning it stress-f
 ree! Our relaxed\, beginner-friendly class is the ideal starting point. Yo
 u don’t need a partner\, nor any dance experience!\n\nIn this class you 
 will learn:\n\nBasic directional steps that form the foundation of salsa.\
 n\nProper frame for comfortable and effective partner-work.\n\nSimple\, ea
 sy-to-remember turn patterns.\n\nGet ready to learn the fundamentals and h
 ave a great time!\n\n**Details:**\n\n**No partner necessary**—rotations 
 ensure everyone dances\n\nPlease wear **non-marking shoes** to protect t
 he floor\n\nArrive 10 minutes early\; warm up and settle in\n\n**When:** 
 Saturday\, 10:00 am – 11:00 am\n\n**Where:** 4140 Redwood Highway #8\, 
 San Rafael\, CA
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8\, San Rafael\, CA
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-beginners-saturday/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
