BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All My Heart This Night Rejoices: The Old World Carolers in Concer
 t
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T150000
UID:261110viEIxhe9cESo6WbF7zvONA
DESCRIPTION:Since 1985\, Sebastopol’s Old World Carolers has evolved fro
 m a few folks caroling during the holidays to a choir with a repertoire of
  hundreds of songs\, but with the same authentic holiday spirit.\n\nThis y
 ear the program includes carols from England\, Wales\, France\, Germany\, 
 Spain\, and Denmark. The public is always invited to sing along\, and song
  sheets are provided for the entire concert. The second part of the concer
 t includes well-known standards for singing along. The beneficiary this ye
 ar is Doctors Without Borders\, a high-rated 501(c)(3) tax-deductible nonp
 rofit bringing medical assistance to Gaza\, Sudan\, and many other places 
 worldwide. Listen to samples and see a photo gallery at traditionalfun.or
 g/owc. TraditionalFun is a site that includes various traditional singing 
 and dancing activities\, which all promote international peace and friends
 hip and can be done locally\, without technology or special equipment.
LOCATION:Sebastopol United Methodist Church
URL:http://traditionalfun.org/owc.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:15 Year Christmas Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T160000
UID:261110uyisee1blUGQIsuHlhVmfw
DESCRIPTION:Come join Kyle Craft - Violinist in a '15 Year Anniversary Chr
 istmas Celebration.' Kyle Craft - Violinist\, most popular for his sold ou
 t 'Afternoon in Vienna' shows\, showcasing the Music and Ambience of 19th 
 Century Vienna\, celebrates 15 Years on Stage. Music Selections include Ho
 liday Classics such as Irving Berlin's 'White Christmas\,' Franz Gruber's 
 'Stille Nacht - Silent Night' and Johann Strauss's 'Frühlingstimmenwalzer
  - Voices of Springs Waltz.'
LOCATION:Kenwood Community Church
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/15-year-christmas-celeb
 ration/20382036/2026-12-06T15
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All My Heart This Night Rejoices: The Old World Carolers in Concer
 t
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T150000
UID:261110WCbhCPLidky8gVwzOn3Gpg
DESCRIPTION:Since 1985\, Sebastopol’s Old World Carolers has evolved fro
 m a few folks caroling during the holidays to a choir with a repertoire of
  hundreds of songs\, but with the same authentic holiday spirit. They have
  continued to sing for peace and justice\, green energy\, human rights\, a
 nimal shelters\, homeless shelters\, shut-ins\, guide dogs\, and many othe
 r benefits for the planet and the community\, the main benefit being the p
 reservation of rare and beautiful songs in people's homes and lives. Songs
  and carols are presented in a simple way so they can be taken home by lis
 teners and sung around the house\, becoming a part of family traditions.\n
 \nHistory is an important part of OWC: learning about cultures through the
 ir languages\, traditions\, and songs\, including Basque\, Spanish\, Itali
 an\, Catalan\, Danish\, Swedish\, Norwegian\, Czech\, Ukrainian\, Old Fren
 ch\, Sicilian\, Hebrew\, Croatian\, German\, Russian\, Bulgarian\, Greek\,
  Welsh\, English\, Gaelic\, and others. They arrange many of the songs the
 y sing\, researching harmonies and styles that are proper for the place an
 d period involved. And of course\, they research and share clothing from d
 ifferent periods and regions! The usual costuming is 19th-century Europe\,
  but they have been known to branch into earlier time periods and exotic l
 ocales for special themed events.\n\nThis year the program includes carols
  from England\, Wales\, France\, Germany\, Spain\, and Denmark. The public
  is always invited to sing along\, and song sheets are provided for the en
 tire concert. The second part of the concert includes well-known standards
  for singing along. This is OWC's 41st year of singing for good causes in 
 Sebastopol. By donating at the concert or purchasing CDs\, listeners can p
 articipate in the true holiday spirit of giving to those who need it. The 
 beneficiary this year is Doctors Without Borders\, a high-rated 501\\(c\\)
 \\(3\\) tax-deductible nonprofit bringing medical assistance to Gaza\, Sud
 an\, and many other places worldwide\, as well as Methodist charities. Lis
 ten to samples and see a photo gallery at traditionalfun.org/owc. Traditi
 onalFun is a site that includes various traditional singing and dancing ac
 tivities\, which all promote international peace and friendship and can be
  done locally\, without technology or special equipment.
LOCATION:Sebastopol United Methodist Church
URL:http://traditionalfun.org/owc.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
