DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T160000
UID:261106y5ysMrT8oUauEekZgC6rZQ
DESCRIPTION:Step into Santa Rosa’s premier winter wonderland for the 6th
  Annual Merry & Bright!\n\nPresented by Sonoma Clean Power\, produced by t
 he Redwood Ice Theatre Company \\(RITC\\)\, and hosted at iconic Snoopy’
 s Home Ice\, this cherished holiday tradition returns with nine completely
  free outdoor ice skating shows. Gather the family to watch dazzling routi
 nes from professional skaters\, accompanied by classic holiday music and s
 easonal entertainment designed to bring neighbors together across Sonoma a
 nd Mendocino counties.\n\nIn the spirit of innovation and sustainability\,
  this year’s outdoor production is powered directly by Sonoma Clean Powe
 r’s all-electric Ford F-150 Lightning truck—showcasing clean energy in
  action while helping local households discover easy ways to save energy t
 his winter.\n\nAdmission: Completely free\, no tickets required!\n\nLocati
 on: Snoopy’s Home Ice\, Santa Rosa\n\nShow Schedule \\(9 Free Outdoor Pe
 rformances\\):\n\nFriday\, December 4: 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p.m.\n\nSaturday\,
  December 5: 2:00 p.m.\, 3:00 p.m.\, 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p.m.\n\nSunday\, Dec
 ember 6: 1:00 p.m.\, 2:00 p.m. & 3:00 p.m.\n\nPro Tip: Arrive early to bun
 dle up\, grab a hot cocoa\, and secure the best spot to watch the show!\n\
 nTo learn more about how SCP is giving back this holiday season\, visit: h
 ttps://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
LOCATION:Snoopy's Home Ice
URL:https://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rooted
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T163000
UID:261106pEVTnLbQTk61EJaF2Rcv4w
DESCRIPTION:This holiday season\, Spreckels Theatre Company offers a heart
 warming alternative to traditional seasonal fare with *Rooted*\, a story a
 bout the messy\, fierce love that keeps us grounded. An intelligent\, gent
 le comedy by Deborah Zoe Laufer\, *Rooted* plays Nov. 27 – Dec.13!\n\nEm
 ery is perfectly content living in her beloved treehouse\, completely isol
 ated from the world\, communing with her plants. Meanwhile\, down on the g
 round\, her sister Hazel is thoroughly miserable\, slaving away at a dead-
 end diner job just to survive and financially support Emery’s eccentric 
 lifestyle. Looking on from the sidelines\, Luanne is yearning for somethin
 g\, anything to bring true meaning into her life.\n\n﻿The sisters' fragi
 le ecosystem is completely upended when Emery’s YouTube videos documenti
 ng her plant experiments unexpectedly go viral. Almost overnight\, her dig
 ital musings accidentally incite a full-blown CULT(!). As throngs of devot
 ed truth-seekers congregate below the treehouse\, the lives of all three w
 omen are plunged into chaos\, compelling each woman to choose their own pa
 th and find their bliss.\n\n*Pick-Your-Price Night: purchase sliding scale
  tickets starting at $10 each for the opening Friday night\, Nov. 27th.*
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts - Bette Condiotti Experi
 mental Theatre
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/rooted/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
