BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T170000
UID:261004U8AiOTBsXE6iYa4sht30zw
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reimagining the Rain in Adobe Creek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T193000
UID:26111310Vtm3i6bkq__L0MU7O1gQ
DESCRIPTION:*Si hablas español\, habrá un intérprete en este evento. In
 dícanoslo en el último paso al inscribirte en el evento.*\n\n***What wou
 ld it look like if our neighborhoods were designed to work with and welcom
 e water instead of sending it away?***\n\nAs a part of our **Harvest the R
 ain Pilot Program**\, Daily Acts is inviting Petaluma community members wh
 o live near or are frequent visitors in the **Adobe Creek** area to **RE
 IMAGINE THE RAIN** by attending an interactive\, neighborhood-based commun
 ity input session.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\n\n**Join this Community Input Session to:**\n\n*\\-Help us underst
 and your experience with stormwater*\n\n*\\-Learn from local experts in ou
 r community*\n\n*\\-Connect with your neighbors over* ***FREE dinner***\n\
 n*\\-Provide feedback on DIY rain garden and curb cut templates*\n\n*\\-En
 ter a* ***gift card drawing*** *for local businesses like The Seed Bank\,
  Caffeine Inc.\, and Refill Mercantile*\n\nDuring the session\, we'll disc
 uss **how we can** **work with rainwater** to build resilient neighborhood
 s. We’ll hear from you to learn where you’ve noticed water pooling in 
 your neighborhood\, and explore whether those places are creating challeng
 es\, or if they could be the beginning of an opportunity to work with wate
 r in an exciting new way! We will also gather your feedback on the rain ga
 rden and curb-cut landscape templates we’re developing. \n\n\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n***lf you live near or 
 frequent Adobe Creek\, we want to hear from you!***\n\nCome share your o
 bservations\, what you’d like to see in your neighborhood\, and any ques
 tions\, excitement or concerns you may have about this pilot program. We h
 ope to see you there!\n\n*Questions? Please email* ***moreinfo@dailyacts.
 org*** *or call* ***(707) 200-8364***
LOCATION:Petaluma Community Center
URL:https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/adobecreek/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Belly Dancing with Raja - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T120000
UID:261107Bg0XHp7E_U6B5V-mdp6bVg
DESCRIPTION:DATE AND TIME: Tuesdays @ 11:00 AM\n\nUnlock your inner streng
 th and find your flow. Belly dancing with Raja is an innovative fusion cl
 ass that blends the rhythmic artistry of belly dance with the high-energ
 y benefits of aerobics. Designed to be both a cardiovascular challenge an
 d a deep toning session\, this class focuses on the “powerhouse” of th
 e body—your core.\n\nBy layering fluid\, isolative movements over an ath
 letic aerobic base\, you will challenge your muscles in ways traditional g
 ym workouts can’t reach.\n\nWhat to Expect in Belly Dancing Class\n\n•
  Core-Centric Power: Use undulations and shimmies to engage deep abdomina
 l muscles for a tighter\, stronger midsection.\n\n• Functional Stability
 : Improve your balance and posture through controlled\, hip-driven moveme
 nts and low-impact aerobic footwork.\n\n• Total Body Toning: Build lean
  muscle in your legs\, glutes\, and arms while maintaining a constant\, he
 art-pumping pace.\n\n• Mind-Body Connection: Enhance your coordination 
 and body awareness through rhythmic\, expressive choreography.\n\n“Wheth
 er you’re looking to define your waistline or simply want a workout that
  feels like a celebration\, this class offers the perfect balance of sweat
  and grace.”\n\nDifficulty Level: All levels welcome! No prior dance ex
 perience is required—just bring your energy and a willingness to move.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/belly-dancing-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
