BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin Farmers Markets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T130000
UID:261113oh1C6FExKkmKF8o5KurwCw
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free Sponsor: Marin Center\n\nWe are hosting our annual
  pie backing contest at the farmers market\,Thursday Pie Baking Contest RS
 VP Explore the bounty of summer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste vine-r
 ipened tomatoes\, corn that was picked that morning\, an d peaches so juic
 y you have to bend over just to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-fed be
 ef\, artisan cheeses\, raw milk\, and freshly baked b reads complete the s
 hopping experience. Specialty prepared foods and handmade art add to the m
 agic of the market. Enjoy the intimate feeling of the Thursday Marin Farme
 rs Market\, an ideal place to meet for lunch and pick up fresh produce for
  the weekend. Discover the abundance and diversity of product at the celeb
 rated Sunday Marin Farmers Market\, the third largest farmers market in Ca
 lifornia. Turn your dollar into a vote for local sustainable agriculture\,
  shrink your eco-footprint\, and revi ve the feeling of being intimately c
 onnected to your food by meeting your farmers face-to-face. The market tak
 es place rain or shine.  www.aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin Veterans' Memorial Auditorium
URL:https://www.marincounty.org/main/calendar#/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T170000
UID:261004aTsJ_uTnzEeI2gQGbfV7XQ
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reimagining the Rain in Washington Creek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T193000
UID:261113jfulU1bX0Ee7BilK5nRrSQ
DESCRIPTION:*Si hablas español\, habrá un intérprete en este evento. In
 dícanoslo en el último paso al inscribirte en el evento.*\n\n***What wou
 ld it look like if our neighborhoods were designed to work with and welcom
 e water instead of sending it away?***\n\nAs a part of our **Harvest the R
 ain Pilot Program**\, Daily Acts is inviting Petaluma community members wh
 o live near or are frequent visitors in the **Washington Creek** area to
  **REIMAGINE THE RAIN** by attending an interactive\, neighborhood-based c
 ommunity input session.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**Join this Com
 munity Input Session to:**\n\n*\\-Help us understand your experience with 
 stormwater*\n\n*\\-Learn from local experts in our community*\n\n*\\-Conne
 ct with your neighbors over* ***FREE dinner***\n\n*\\-Provide feedback on 
 DIY rain garden and curb cut templates*\n\n*\\-Enter a* ***gift card draw
 ing*** *for local businesses like Petaluma Coffee & Tea\, Caffeine Inc.\, 
 Refill Mercantile and The Seed Bank!*\n\nDuring the session\, we'll discus
 s **how we can** **work with rainwater** to build resilient neighborhoods.
  We’ll hear from you to learn where you’ve noticed water pooling in yo
 ur neighborhood\, and explore whether those places are creating challenges
 \, or if they could be the beginning of an opportunity to work with water 
 in an exciting new way! We will also gather your feedback on the rain gard
 en and curb-cut landscape templates we’re developing. \n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n***lf you live near or frequent Washington Creek
 \, we want to hear from you!***\n\nCome share your observations\, what you
 ’d like to see in your neighborhood\, and any questions\, excitement or 
 concerns you may have about this pilot program. We hope to see you there!\
 n\n*Questions? Please email* ***moreinfo@dailyacts.org*** *or call* ***(7
 07) 200-8364***
LOCATION:Petaluma Community Center (Lucchesi)
URL:https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/washingtoncreek/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
