BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ORGONE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T200000
UID:2610315AnyEzFEUUm-3sy5NPGhyA
DESCRIPTION:For nearly twenty years ORGŌNE \\(a universal life force\, pr
 onounced or-gōne\\) has churned out gritty funk and soul recordings and t
 oured relentlessly across the United States and Europe. Traditionally both
  the studio and live iterations of the band drew on a tight-knit collectiv
 e of the West Coast’s finest funk and soul musicians—although founding
  members Sergio Rios \\(guitar/engineer\\) and Dan Hastie \\(keyboards\\) 
 have been constant anchors. Since late 2013\, Rios and Hastie have been jo
 ined by Dale Jennings \\(bass\\) and Sam Halterman \\(drums\\) to form a p
 ermanent nucleus.\n\nORGŌNE’s accolades are too long to list in entiret
 y. ORGŌNE’s live show captivates audiences and packs dance floors—whe
 ther it’s on sold out headlining tours\; sharing the stage with The Root
 s\, Al Green\, Sharon Jones & the Dap-Kings\, and Galactic\; or appearance
 s at festivals like Bonnaroo\, New Orleans Jazz Fest\, High Sierra\, Bear 
 Creek\, and Jam Cruise. The well-traveled band has released albums on Ubiq
 uity\, Shanachie\, and Colemine Records and served as the studio band on h
 its like Alicia Keys’ “Teenage Love Affair” and Cee Lo Green’s Gra
 mmy-winning “Fool For You.” Critics like NPR and Jambase don’t shy a
 way from heaping praise on a group with “irresistible funkiness and abil
 ity to transcend genre” \\(LA Weekly\\).\n\nSince ORGŌNE released their
  album Connection on 3 Palm Records\, and distributed by Colemine Records 
 and Secretly Distribution\, they have released multiple singles including 
 their cover of “It’s My Thing”\, featuring Adryon de Leon. Their sec
 ond LP from 3 Palm Records was releases in 2021\, Moonshadows\; featuring 
 multiple artists from the Orgone family to create a flying high blend of l
 ate 70’s California soul and funky rock.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040669990?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Winter Wonder Lantern Walks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T183000
UID:261023jLMAPW4cdEKeZgOLN040nQ
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the beauty and quiet magic of the season during Wint
 er Wonder Lantern Walks\, a festive after-dark experience at Sonoma Botani
 cal Garden. Guided along the route by Garden staff and volunteers\, guests
  will stroll through the winter landscape carrying glowing lanterns\, disc
 overing softly shadowed pathways\, towering trees\, and the peaceful still
 ness of the Garden beneath the night sky. Rather than a traditional docent
 -led tour\, this experience is designed as a peaceful and immersive opport
 unity to enjoy the rare experience of walking through the Garden after hou
 rs and after dark. Along the way\, enjoy moments of reflection\, seasonal 
 ambiance\, and the simple joy of gathering outdoors during the holiday sea
 son.\n\nThe evening begins with hot cocoa\, spiced cider\, wine tasting an
 d cookies from 5:30–6:00 p.m.\, followed by a brief welcome and lantern 
 walk orientation before departing together for a guided walk through the G
 arden.\n\nWinter Wonder Lantern Walks are a seasonal fundraiser that will 
 support the Garden’s programs\, collections\, and conservation efforts. 
 PLEASE READ the important accessibility and experience information\, along
  with the registration and cancellation policy below before purchasing tic
 kets.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/lantern-walks/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carlos Herrera Band
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T193000
UID:26102222Z96sF4x0aMrfgCMQk6rg
DESCRIPTION:Date: Friday\, December 11\, 2026\n\nTime: Doors 6:30 PM\, S
 how 7:30 PM\n\nTickets: Free\n\nFood Vendor: Smash'd Burger Bar\n\n21\\+ 
 Only\n\nLocation: Coyote Sonoma - 44F Mill Street\, Healdsburg CA\, 95448\
 n\nCarlos Herrera features Latin Music encompassing diverse styles ranging
  from its colonial roots to popular influences\, with emphasis on music fr
 om Latin America. Noted for his guitar music and vocals but\, more for his
  improvisations and his uncanny ability to extemporize. Herrera hales from
  Costa Rica where he began his music career at a very early age. After man
 y years playing around Latin America with his band he moved to The United 
 States where he now resides in Sonoma Valley.
LOCATION:Coyote Sonoma
URL:https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/carlos-herrera-band-1211-p267.aspx
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
