BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fright Night with Cameron Pierce & David Agranoff
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T200000
UID:261110rq1sNGpjEEyYBP8wcV3ElQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us at 6 pm on SATURDAY\, DECEMBER 12 for another FRIGHT 
 NIGHT author event with readings\, Q&A\, and signings.\n\nThis time we're 
 featuring CAMERON PIERCE in conversation with DAVID AGRANOFF for an eveni
 ng of bizarro literature. With Ross E. Lockhart moderating\, it's sure to
  be a fascinating discussion.\n\nCameron Pierce's new novel Most Things Ha
 ven't Worked Out\, just published by CLASH Books\, is a coming of age stor
 y about the painful pursuit of love\, fortune\, and fame reading like an o
 ptimistic Jesus' Son for a new generation. Told through a series of follie
 s\, Pierce presents a journey of finding agency from someone who doesn't h
 ave an inkling of what they want out of life.\n\nDavid Agranoff's latest C
 LASH novel\, The Last Night to Kill Nazis\, is an emotional rollercoaster
  of adventure\, terror and revenge that explores one of the world's most e
 vil events through the lens of a horror novel. An entertaining and enlight
 ening novel that is Inglorious Basterds meets Dracula. Watch for the seque
 l The Next Night to Kill Nazis coming in January!
LOCATION:Word Horde Emporium
URL:https://www.weirdandfantastic.com/events/6745620261212
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rooted
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T220000
UID:261106v8dduXX8-U6KTQAzA4eQeg
DESCRIPTION:This holiday season\, Spreckels Theatre Company offers a heart
 warming alternative to traditional seasonal fare with *Rooted*\, a story a
 bout the messy\, fierce love that keeps us grounded. An intelligent\, gent
 le comedy by Deborah Zoe Laufer\, *Rooted* plays Nov. 27 – Dec.13!\n\nEm
 ery is perfectly content living in her beloved treehouse\, completely isol
 ated from the world\, communing with her plants. Meanwhile\, down on the g
 round\, her sister Hazel is thoroughly miserable\, slaving away at a dead-
 end diner job just to survive and financially support Emery’s eccentric 
 lifestyle. Looking on from the sidelines\, Luanne is yearning for somethin
 g\, anything to bring true meaning into her life.\n\n﻿The sisters' fragi
 le ecosystem is completely upended when Emery’s YouTube videos documenti
 ng her plant experiments unexpectedly go viral. Almost overnight\, her dig
 ital musings accidentally incite a full-blown CULT(!). As throngs of devot
 ed truth-seekers congregate below the treehouse\, the lives of all three w
 omen are plunged into chaos\, compelling each woman to choose their own pa
 th and find their bliss.\n\n*Pick-Your-Price Night: purchase sliding scale
  tickets starting at $10 each for the opening Friday night\, Nov. 27th.*
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts - Bette Condiotti Experi
 mental Theatre
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/rooted/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T170000
UID:261106CgwS8E5WSkORz9_keTdsXg
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Montagne Russe Winery and Record Lounge
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108833618?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
