BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pairings for the Senses
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T180000
UID:2611107W6G61ynBk--XNB0_g-0Cg
DESCRIPTION:ART \\+ POETRY \\+ WINE SVMA’s poetry pairing returns! Join 
 poets Molly Bendall\, Jennifer Hasegawa\, and Timothy Nolan as they read t
 heir work\, including new poems written in conversation with works by M. L
 ouise Stanley in the exhibition. Sip wine from female-owned wineries as we
  celebrate feminism\, wit\, art\, and alter egos. Sunday\, December 13\, 4
 -6 PM $55 members\, $65 non-members Pre-registration is required.
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1101121869590888/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rooted
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T163000
UID:261106vfMY8UUDvkKAFABQ-Nd4mg
DESCRIPTION:This holiday season\, Spreckels Theatre Company offers a heart
 warming alternative to traditional seasonal fare with *Rooted*\, a story a
 bout the messy\, fierce love that keeps us grounded. An intelligent\, gent
 le comedy by Deborah Zoe Laufer\, *Rooted* plays Nov. 27 – Dec.13!\n\nEm
 ery is perfectly content living in her beloved treehouse\, completely isol
 ated from the world\, communing with her plants. Meanwhile\, down on the g
 round\, her sister Hazel is thoroughly miserable\, slaving away at a dead-
 end diner job just to survive and financially support Emery’s eccentric 
 lifestyle. Looking on from the sidelines\, Luanne is yearning for somethin
 g\, anything to bring true meaning into her life.\n\n﻿The sisters' fragi
 le ecosystem is completely upended when Emery’s YouTube videos documenti
 ng her plant experiments unexpectedly go viral. Almost overnight\, her dig
 ital musings accidentally incite a full-blown CULT(!). As throngs of devot
 ed truth-seekers congregate below the treehouse\, the lives of all three w
 omen are plunged into chaos\, compelling each woman to choose their own pa
 th and find their bliss.\n\n*Pick-Your-Price Night: purchase sliding scale
  tickets starting at $10 each for the opening Friday night\, Nov. 27th.*
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts - Bette Condiotti Experi
 mental Theatre
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/rooted/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annual Lucia Jul Fika with Linnea Lodge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T160000
UID:261106Cer0Hz9zPEOUPWtRMTT6eQ
DESCRIPTION:Come celebrate Scandinavian holiday traditions with Linnea Lod
 ge!\n\nLinnea Lodge #504 invites Members\, families\, friends\, and those 
 interested in Scandinavian holiday traditions to come participate in our a
 nnual **Lucia Jul Fika.**\n\nA Swedish "fika" is a break in the day to en
 joy coffee and a treat. We're taking fika and adding our annual Santa Luci
 a pageant and other Jul traditions for a day of cultural fellowship. Enjoy
  live music\, dancing around the tree\, a gift basket drawing\, and a spec
 ial visit from Jultomten (Santa!) to complete the festivities.\\*\\*\n\nCo
 ffee\, tea\, and soft drinks will be served\, along with sandwiches\, chee
 se and crackerbread\, fruit\, cookies\, and traditional Swedish lussekatte
 r (saffron buns).\n\n**What to bring:**\n\n\\- Members: Please bring 1 sma
 ll Poinsettia for tables and a dozen cookies or a baked treat for our Fika
 \n\n\\- \\*\\*For everyone bringing children\, please bring a small wrappe
 d gift for each child in your party with their **name printed clearly on 
 the package.** *(Drop off packages discretely at check in.)*\n\nChildren 
 participating in the pageant are asked to arrive at 1:30 PM for practice. 
 Participating boys should wear black pants and a white shirt. Gowns provid
 ed.\n\n***Seating is limited. Please RSVP by December 2nd.***
LOCATION:Petaluma Veterans Memorial Building 
URL:https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/swedish-lucia-fika
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:HOLIDAY MOSAIC
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T170000
UID:261029U78r_VKsJEelOA1LIVqXGA
DESCRIPTION:Sing Napa Valley presents Holiday Mosaic\, a festive and inspi
 ring choral celebration of the seasons traditions throughout the US and ar
 ound the world. The program features Camille Saint-Saëns' beloved Christm
 as Oratorio\, performed with vocal soloists\, chorus\, organ\, strings\, a
 nd harp\, alongside music honoring Canukah\, Kwanzaa\, Las Posadas\, the W
 inter Solstice\, and other holiday traditions.\n\nAudiences will enjoy spi
 rited multicultural selections\, a holiday sing-along\, and a special appe
 arance from a familiar seasonal guest. Conducted by Ronnie Zanella\, the c
 oncert showcases Sing Napa Valley's 50-member intergenerational choir in a
  joyful celebration of community\, culture\, and the season
LOCATION:First United Methodist Church
URL:https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/holiday-mosaic-2
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
